#: ../../library/os.rst:186
msgid ""
"A :term:`mapping` object where keys and values are strings that represent "
"the process environment.  For example, ``environ['HOME']`` is the pathname "
"of your home directory (on some platforms), and is equivalent to "
"``getenv(\"HOME\")`` in C."
msgstr ""
"Predmet :term:`mapping` objekt, kde klice a hodnoty jsou retezce, ktere "
"reprezentuji prostredi procesu. Naprikliad, ``environ['HOME']`` je cesta "
"vaseho domovske slozky (na nektere platformach) a je ekvivalentni s "
"``getenv(\"HOME\")`` v C."

#: ../../library/os.rst:191
msgid ""
"This mapping is captured the first time the :mod:`os` module is imported, "
"typically during Python startup as part of processing :file:`site.py`.  "
"Changes to the environment made after this time are not reflected in "
":data:`os.environ`, except for changes made by modifying :data:`os.environ` "
"directly."
msgstr ""
"Toto mapovani je zachyceno pri prvnim importu modulu :mod:`os`, typicky "
"behem spusteni Pythonu jako cast zpracovani :file:`site.py`. Zmeny prostredi"
" provedene po teto dobe se neodrazi v :data:`os.environ`, pokud nejsou zmeny"
" provedeny modifikaci :data:`os.environ` primo."

#: ../../library/os.rst:196
msgid ""
"This mapping may be used to modify the environment as well as query the "
"environment.  :func:`putenv` will be called automatically when the mapping "
"is modified."
msgstr ""
"Toto mapovani moze byt pouzito k modifikaci prostredi a take k dotazovani na"
" prostredi. :func:`putenv` bude automaticky volana pri zmene mapovani."

#: ../../library/os.rst:200
msgid ""
"On Unix, keys and values use :func:`sys.getfilesystemencoding` and "
"``'surrogateescape'`` error handler. Use :data:`environb` if you would like "
"to use a different encoding."
msgstr ""
"Na Unixu klice a hodnoty pouzivaji :func:`sys.getfilesystemencoding` a "
"``'surrogateescape'`` obsluhovani chyby. Pouzijte :data:`environb`, pokud "
"chcete pouzit jine kodovani."

#: ../../library/os.rst:204
msgid ""
"On Windows, the keys are converted to uppercase. This also applies when "
"getting, setting, or deleting an item. For example, ``environ['monty'] = "
"'python'`` maps the key ``'MONTY'`` to the value ``'python'``."
msgstr ""
"Na Windows klice jsou konvertovany na velka pismena. To se take vztahuje pri"
" ziskavani, nastavovani nebo smazani polozky. Naprikliad, ``environ['monty']"
" = 'python'`` mapuje klic ``'MONTY'`` na hodnotu ``'python'``."

#: ../../library/os.rst:211
msgid ""
"Calling :func:`putenv` directly does not change :data:`os.environ`, so it's "
"better to modify :data:`os.environ`."
msgstr ""
"Primy volan :func:`putenv` nemenimenit :data:`os.environ`, takze je lepsi "
"modifikovat :data:`os.environ`."

#: ../../library/os.rst:216
msgid ""
"On some platforms, including FreeBSD and macOS, setting ``environ`` may "
"cause memory leaks.  Refer to the system documentation for "
":c:func:`!putenv`."
msgstr ""
"Na nekterych platformach, vcetne FreeBSD a macOS, nastavovani ``environ`` "
"muze zpusobit unik pameti. Podivejte se do systemove dokumentace pro "
":c:func:`!putenv`."

#: ../../library/os.rst:220
msgid ""
"You can delete items in this mapping to unset environment variables. "
":func:`unsetenv` will be called automatically when an item is deleted from "
":data:`os.environ`, and when one of the :meth:`pop` or :meth:`clear` methods"
" is called."
msgstr ""
"Muzete smazat polozky v tomto mapovani na zruseni promennnych prostredi. "
":func:`unsetenv` bude automaticky volana pri smazani polozky z "
":data:`os.environ` a pri volani jedne z metod :meth:`pop` nebo "
":meth:`clear`."

#: ../../library/os.rst:227
msgid "The :func:`os.reload_environ` function."
msgstr "Funkce :func:`os.reload_environ`."

#: ../../library/os.rst:229 ../../library/os.rst:245
msgid ""
"Updated to support :pep:`584`'s merge (``|``) and update (``|=``) operators."
msgstr ""
"Aktualizovano pro podporu :pep:`584` mergovani (``|``) a aktualizace "
"(``|=``) operatory."

#: ../../library/os.rst:235
msgid ""
"Bytes version of :data:`environ`: a :term:`mapping` object where both keys "
"and values are :class:`bytes` objects representing the process environment. "
":data:`environ` and :data:`environb` are synchronized (modifying "
":data:`environb` updates :data:`environ`, and vice versa)."
msgstr ""
"Verze v bajtech :data:`environ`: predmet :term:`mapping` objekt, kde jsou "
"oba klice a hodnoty objekty :class:`bytes` reprezentujici prostredi procesu."
" :data:`environ` a :data:`environb` jsou synchronizovany (modifikace "
":data:`environb` aktualizuje :data:`environ` a naopak)."

#: ../../library/os.rst:240
msgid ""
":data:`environb` is only available if :const:`supports_bytes_environ` is "
"``True``."
msgstr ""
":data:`environb` je k dispozici pouze pokud :const:`supports_bytes_environ` "
"je ``True``."

#: ../../library/os.rst:251
msgid ""
"The :data:`os.environ` and :data:`os.environb` mappings are a cache of "
"environment variables at the time that Python started. As such, changes to "
"the current process environment are not reflected if made outside Python, or"
" by :func:`os.putenv` or :func:`os.unsetenv`. Use :func:`!os.reload_environ`"
" to update :data:`os.environ` and :data:`os.environb` with any such changes "
"to the current process environment."
msgstr ""
"Mapovani :data:`os.environ` a :data:`os.environb` jsou mezipameti "
"promennnych prostredi v dobe, kdy byl Python spusten. Jak jsou zmeny v "
"aktualnim prostredi procesu se neprojevy, pokud jsou provedeny vne Pythonu "
"nebo :func:`os.putenv` nebo :func:`os.unsetenv`. Pouzijte "
":func:`!os.reload_environ` k aktualizaci :data:`os.environ` a "
":data:`os.environb` s takymito zmenami v aktualnim prostredi procesu."

#: ../../library/os.rst:259
msgid ""
"This function is not thread-safe. Calling it while the environment is being "
"modified in an other thread is an undefined behavior. Reading from "
":data:`os.environ` or :data:`os.environb`, or calling :func:`os.getenv` "
"while reloading, may return an empty result."
msgstr ""
"Tato funkce neni vlakno-bezpecna. Volani ji zatimco se prostredi modifikuje "
"v jinem vlakne je nedefinovane chovani. Cteni z :data:`os.environ` nebo "
":data:`os.environb` nebo volani :func:`os.getenv` zatimco se nacita, muze "
"vratit prazdny vysledek."

#: ../../library/os.rst:272
msgid "These functions are described in :ref:`os-file-dir`."
msgstr "Tyto funkce jsou popsany v :ref:`os-file-dir`."

#: ../../library/os.rst:277
msgid ""
"Encode :term:`path-like <path-like object>` *filename* to the "
":term:`filesystem encoding and error handler`; return :class:`bytes` "
"unchanged."
msgstr ""
"Zakoduj :term:`cestu podobnou <path-like object>` *filename* na "
":term:`kodovani systemu souboru a obsluhovani chyb`; vrati :class:`bytes` "
"beze zmen."

#: ../../library/os.rst:281
msgid ":func:`fsdecode` is the reverse function."
msgstr ":func:`fsdecode` je opacna funkce."

#: ../../library/os.rst:285 ../../library/os.rst:300
msgid ""
"Support added to accept objects implementing the :class:`os.PathLike` "
"interface."
msgstr ""
"Podpora pridana pro prijem objektu implementujicich rozhrani "
":class:`os.PathLike`."

#: ../../library/os.rst:292
msgid ""
"Decode the :term:`path-like <path-like object>` *filename* from the "
":term:`filesystem encoding and error handler`; return :class:`str` "
"unchanged."
msgstr ""
"Dekoduj :term:`cestu podobnou <path-like object>` *filename* z "
":term:`kodovani systemu souboru a obsluhovani chyb`; vrati :class:`str` beze"
" zmen."

#: ../../library/os.rst:296
msgid ":func:`fsencode` is the reverse function."
msgstr ":func:`fsencode` je opacna funkce."

#: ../../library/os.rst:307
msgid "Return the file system representation of the path."
msgstr "Vrati reprezentaci cesty systemu souboru."

#: ../../library/os.rst:309
msgid ""
"If :class:`str` or :class:`bytes` is passed in, it is returned unchanged. "
"Otherwise :meth:`~os.PathLike.__fspath__` is called and its value is "
"returned as long as it is a :class:`str` or :class:`bytes` object. In all "
"other cases, :exc:`TypeError` is raised."
msgstr ""
"Pokud je predan :class:`str` nebo :class:`bytes`, je vracen beze zmen. Jinak"
" :meth:`~os.PathLike.__fspath__` je volana a jeji hodnota je vracena pokud "
"je to :class:`str` nebo :class:`bytes` objekt. Ve vsech ostatnich pripadech "
"je vyvolvana :exc:`TypeError`."

#: ../../library/os.rst:319
msgid ""
"An :term:`abstract base class` for objects representing a file system path, "
"e.g. :class:`pathlib.PurePath`."
msgstr ""
"Predmet :term:`abstract base class` pro objekty reprezentujici cestu systemu"
" souboru, např. :class:`pathlib.PurePath`."

#: ../../library/os.rst:327
msgid "Return the file system path representation of the object."
msgstr "Vrati reprezentaci cesty systemu souboru objektu."

#: ../../library/os.rst:329
msgid ""
"The method should only return a :class:`str` or :class:`bytes` object, with "
"the preference being for :class:`str`."
msgstr ""
"Metoda by mela vratit pouze :class:`str` nebo :class:`bytes` objekt, s "
"uprednostenim :class:`str`."

#: ../../library/os.rst:335
msgid ""
"Return the value of the environment variable *key* as a string if it exists,"
" or *default* if it doesn't. *key* is a string. Note that since "
":func:`getenv` uses :data:`os.environ`, the mapping of :func:`getenv` is "
"similarly also captured on import, and the function may not reflect future "
"environment changes."
msgstr ""
"Vrati hodnotu promenne prostredi *key* jako retezec pokud existuje nebo "
"*default* pokud neexistuje. *key* je retezec. Vezmetev na vedomí, ze "
":func:`getenv` pouziva :data:`os.environ`, mapovani :func:`getenv` je "
"podobne zachyceno pri importu a funkce nemuze odraze budouci zmeny "
"prostredi."

#: ../../library/os.rst:341
msgid ""
"On Unix, keys and values are decoded with :func:`sys.getfilesystemencoding` "
"and ``'surrogateescape'`` error handler. Use :func:`os.getenvb` if you would"
" like to use a different encoding."
msgstr ""
"Na Unixu klice a hodnoty jsou dekodirovany s "
":func:`sys.getfilesystemencoding` a ``'surrogateescape'`` obsluhovani chyby."
" Pouzijte :func:`os.getenvb` pokud chcete pouzit jine kodovani."

#: ../../library/os.rst:350
msgid ""
"Return the value of the environment variable *key* as bytes if it exists, or"
" *default* if it doesn't. *key* must be bytes. Note that since "
":func:`getenvb` uses :data:`os.environb`, the mapping of :func:`getenvb` is "
"similarly also captured on import, and the function may not reflect future "
"environment changes."
msgstr ""
"Vrati hodnotu promenne prostredi *key* jako bajty pokud existuje nebo "
"*default* pokud neexistuje. *key* musi byt bajty. Vezmetev na vedomí, ze "
":func:`getenvb` pouziva :data:`os.environb`, mapovani :func:`getenvb` je "
"podobne zachyceno pri importu a funkce nemuze odraze budouci zmeny "
"prostredi."

#: ../../library/os.rst:357
msgid ""
":func:`getenvb` is only available if :const:`supports_bytes_environ` is "
"``True``."
msgstr ""
":func:`getenvb` je k dispozici pouze pokud :const:`supports_bytes_environ` "
"je ``True``."

#: ../../library/os.rst:367
msgid ""
"Returns the list of directories that will be searched for a named "
"executable, similar to a shell, when launching a process. *env*, when "
"specified, should be an environment variable dictionary to lookup the PATH "
"in. By default, when *env* is ``None``, :data:`environ` is used."
msgstr ""
"Vrati seznam adresaru, ktere budou hledany pro pojmenovany spustitelny "
"soubor, podobne jako shell, pri spusteni procesu. *env*, je-li specificen, "
"by mel byt slovnik promenne prostredi pro hledani PATH. Ve vychozim pripade,"
" pokud je *env* ``None``, je pouzit :data:`environ`."

#: ../../library/os.rst:378
msgid ""
"Return the effective group id of the current process.  This corresponds to "
"the \"set id\" bit on the file being executed in the current process."
msgstr ""
"Vrati efektivni id skupiny aktualniho procesu. Toto odpovida \"set id\" bitu"
" v souboru spousteneho v aktualnim procesu."

#: ../../library/os.rst:388
msgid "Return the current process's effective user id."
msgstr "Vrati efektivni id uzivatele aktualniho procesu."

#: ../../library/os.rst:397
msgid "Return the real group id of the current process."
msgstr "Vrati skutecne id skupiny aktualniho procesu."

#: ../../library/os.rst:401 ../../library/os.rst:474 ../../library/os.rst:558
#: ../../library/os.rst:783
msgid ""
"The function is a stub on WASI, see :ref:`wasm-availability` for more "
"information."
msgstr ""
"Funkce je pahyl na WASI, viz :ref:`wasm-availability` pro vice informaci."

#: ../../library/os.rst:407
msgid ""
"Return list of group ids that *user* belongs to. If *group* is not in the "
"list, it is included; typically, *group* is specified as the group ID field "
"from the password record for *user*, because that group ID will otherwise be"
" potentially omitted."
msgstr ""
"Vrati seznam id skupin, kterym patri *user*. Pokud *group* neni v seznamu, "
"je zahrnut; typicky je *group* specifikovan jako pole id skupiny z hesla "
"zaznam pro *user*, protoze to id skupiny by bylo jinak potencialne "
"vynechano."

#: ../../library/os.rst:419
msgid ""
"Return list of supplemental group ids associated with the current process."
msgstr ""
"Vrati seznam doplnkovych id skupin souvisejicich s aktualnim procesem."

#: ../../library/os.rst:425
msgid ""
"On macOS, :func:`getgroups` behavior differs somewhat from other Unix "
"platforms. If the Python interpreter was built with a deployment target of "
"``10.5`` or earlier, :func:`getgroups` returns the list of effective group "
"ids associated with the current user process; this list is limited to a "
"system-defined number of entries, typically 16, and may be modified by calls"
" to :func:`setgroups` if suitably privileged. If built with a deployment "
"target greater than ``10.5``, :func:`getgroups` returns the current group "
"access list for the user associated with the effective user id of the "
"process; the group access list may change over the lifetime of the process, "
"it is not affected by calls to :func:`setgroups`, and its length is not "
"limited to 16.  The deployment target value, "
":const:`MACOSX_DEPLOYMENT_TARGET`, can be obtained with "
":func:`sysconfig.get_config_var`."
msgstr ""
"Na macOS se chovani :func:`getgroups` lisi neco od ostatnich Unix platform. "
"Pokud byl interpret Pythonu sestaven s cilovou verzi nasazeni ``10.5`` nebo "
"driv, :func:`getgroups` vrati seznam efektivnich id skupin souvisejicich s "
"aktualnim procesem uzivatele; tento seznam je omezen na systém-definovany "
"pocet polozek, typicky 16, a moze byt zmenen volani :func:`setgroups` pokud "
"je vhodne privilegovany. Pokud byl sestaven s cilovou verzi nasazeni vetsim "
"nez ``10.5``, :func:`getgroups` vrati aktualni seznam pristupu skupin pro "
"uzivatele souvisejiciho s efektivnim id uzivatele procesu; seznam pristupu "
"skupin se muze zmenit po dobu zivota procesu, neni odraze volani "
":func:`setgroups` a jeho delka neni omezenana na 16. Hodnota cilove verze "
"nasazeni, :const:`MACOSX_DEPLOYMENT_TARGET`, muze byt ziskana s "
":func:`sysconfig.get_config_var`."

#: ../../library/os.rst:442
msgid ""
"Return the name of the user logged in on the controlling terminal of the "
"process.  For most purposes, it is more useful to use "
":func:`getpass.getuser` since the latter checks the environment variables "
":envvar:`LOGNAME` or :envvar:`USERNAME` to find out who the user is, and "
"falls back to ``pwd.getpwuid(os.getuid())[0]`` to get the login name of the "
"current real user id."
msgstr ""
"Vrati jmeno uzivatele prihlaseneho na kontrolovacim terminalu procesu. Pro "
"vetsinu ucelu je uzivatecnejsi pouzit :func:`getpass.getuser` protoze ta "
"kontroluje promenne prostredi :envvar:`LOGNAME` nebo :envvar:`USERNAME` pro "
"zjisteni kdo je uzivatel a pada zpet na ``pwd.getpwuid(os.getuid())[0]`` pro"
" ziskani prihlasovacího jmena aktualniho skutecneho id uzivatele."

#: ../../library/os.rst:454
msgid ""
"Return the process group id of the process with process id *pid*. If *pid* "
"is 0, the process group id of the current process is returned."
msgstr ""
"Vrati id skupiny procesu procesu s id procesu *pid*. Pokud je *pid* 0, je "
"vraceno id skupiny procesu aktualniho procesu."

#: ../../library/os.rst:463
msgid "Return the id of the current process group."
msgstr "Vrati id aktualniho skupiny procesu."

#: ../../library/os.rst:472
msgid "Return the current process id."
msgstr "Vrati id aktualniho procesu."

#: ../../library/os.rst:481
msgid ""
"Return the parent's process id.  When the parent process has exited, on Unix"
" the id returned is the one of the init process (1), on Windows it is still "
"the same id, which may be already reused by another process."
msgstr ""
"Vrati id procesu rodice. Pokud byl proces rodie ukoncen, na Unixu je vratene"
" id jednoznamenne od init procesu (1), na Windows je stale stejne id, ktere "
"mohou byt jiz znovu pouzivano jinym procesem."

#: ../../library/os.rst:487
msgid "Added support for Windows."
msgstr "Pridana podpora pro Windows."

#: ../../library/os.rst:495
msgid ""
"Get program scheduling priority.  The value *which* is one of "
":const:`PRIO_PROCESS`, :const:`PRIO_PGRP`, or :const:`PRIO_USER`, and *who* "
"is interpreted relative to *which* (a process identifier for "
":const:`PRIO_PROCESS`, process group identifier for :const:`PRIO_PGRP`, and "
"a user ID for :const:`PRIO_USER`).  A zero value for *who* denotes "
"(respectively) the calling process, the process group of the calling "
"process, or the real user ID of the calling process."
msgstr ""
"Ziskej prioritu planovani programu. Hodnota *which* je jedna z "
":const:`PRIO_PROCESS`, :const:`PRIO_PGRP`, nebo :const:`PRIO_USER` a *who* "
"je interpretovana vzhledem k *which* (identifikator procesu pro "
":const:`PRIO_PROCESS`, identifikator skupiny procesu pro :const:`PRIO_PGRP` "
"a uzivatelske id pro :const:`PRIO_USER`). Nulova hodnota pro *who* znaci "
"(respektive) volajici proces, skupinu procesu volajiciho procesu nebo "
"skutecne id uzivatele volajiciho procesu."

#: ../../library/os.rst:512 ../../library/os.rst:524
msgid ""
"Parameters for the :func:`getpriority` and :func:`setpriority` functions."
msgstr "Parametry pro funkce :func:`getpriority` a :func:`setpriority`."

#: ../../library/os.rst:532
msgid ""
"Return a tuple (ruid, euid, suid) denoting the current process's real, "
"effective, and saved user ids."
msgstr ""
"Vrati tuple (ruid, euid, suid) znacici aktualni id skutecneho, efektivniho a"
" ulozeneho uzivatele aktualnich procesu."

#: ../../library/os.rst:542
msgid ""
"Return a tuple (rgid, egid, sgid) denoting the current process's real, "
"effective, and saved group ids."
msgstr ""
"Vrati tuple (rgid, egid, sgid) znacici aktualni id skutecne, efektivni a "
"ulozene skupiny aktualnich procesu."

#: ../../library/os.rst:554
msgid "Return the current process's real user id."
msgstr "Vrati skutecne id uzivatele aktualniho procesu."

#: ../../library/os.rst:564
msgid ""
"Call the system ``initgroups()`` to initialize the group access list with "
"all of the groups of which the specified username is a member, plus the "
"specified group id."
msgstr ""
"Vola system ``initgroups()`` pro inicializaci seznamu pristupu skupin vsemi "
"skupinami, kterych clenkem je specifikovany uzivatel, plus specifikovane id "
"skupiny."

#: ../../library/os.rst:577
msgid ""
"Set the environment variable named *key* to the string *value*.  Such "
"changes to the environment affect subprocesses started with "
":func:`os.system`, :func:`popen` or :func:`fork` and :func:`execv`."
msgstr ""
"Nastav promenne prostredi pojmenovane *key* na retezec *value*. Takove zmeny"
" prostredi ovlivnuji podprocesy spustene s :func:`os.system`, :func:`popen` "
"nebo :func:`fork` a :func:`execv`."

#: ../../library/os.rst:581
msgid ""
"Assignments to items in :data:`os.environ` are automatically translated into"
" corresponding calls to :func:`putenv`; however, calls to :func:`putenv` "
"don't update :data:`os.environ`, so it is actually preferable to assign to "
"items of :data:`os.environ`. This also applies to :func:`getenv` and "
":func:`getenvb`, which respectively use :data:`os.environ` and "
":data:`os.environb` in their implementations."
msgstr ""
"Prideleni polozek v :data:`os.environ` jsou automaticky prevedeny na "
"odpovidajici volan :func:`putenv`; nicmene volan :func:`putenv` nemeni "
":data:`os.environ`, takze je vlastne lepsi pridit polozky "
":data:`os.environ`. Toto se take vztahuje na :func:`getenv` a "
":func:`getenvb`, ktere respektive pouzivaji :data:`os.environ` a "
":data:`os.environb` v jejich implementacich."

#: ../../library/os.rst:587 ../../library/os.rst:837
msgid "See also the :func:`os.reload_environ` function."
msgstr "Viz taky funkce :func:`os.reload_environ`."

#: ../../library/os.rst:591
msgid ""
"On some platforms, including FreeBSD and macOS, setting ``environ`` may "
"cause memory leaks. Refer to the system documentation for :c:func:`!putenv`."
msgstr ""
"Na nektere platforme, vcetne FreeBSD a macOS, nastavi ``environ`` muze "
"zpusobit unik pameti. Podivejte se do systemove dokumentace pro "
":c:func:`!putenv`."

#: ../../library/os.rst:594
msgid ""
"Raises an :ref:`auditing event <auditing>` ``os.putenv`` with arguments "
"``key``, ``value``."
msgstr ""
"Vyvola :ref:`auditni udalost <auditing>` ``os.putenv`` s argumenty ``key``, "
"``value``."

#: ../../library/os.rst:596
msgid "The function is now always available."
msgstr "Funkce je nyn vzdy dostupna."

#: ../../library/os.rst:602
msgid "Set the current process's effective group id."
msgstr "Nastav efektivni id skupiny aktualniho procesu."

#: ../../library/os.rst:609
msgid "Set the current process's effective user id."
msgstr "Nastav efektivni id uzivatele aktualniho procesu."

#: ../../library/os.rst:616
msgid "Set the current process' group id."
msgstr "Nastav id skupiny aktualniho procesu."

#: ../../library/os.rst:623
msgid ""
"Set the list of supplemental group ids associated with the current process "
"to *groups*. *groups* must be a sequence, and each element must be an "
"integer identifying a group. This operation is typically available only to "
"the superuser."
msgstr ""
"Nastav seznam doplnkovych id skupin souvisejicich s aktualnim procesem na "
"*groups*. *groups* musi byt sekvence a kazdy prvek musi byt cele cislo "
"identifikujici skupinu. Tato operace je typicky dostupna pouze "
"superuzivateli."

#: ../../library/os.rst:629
msgid ""
"On macOS, the length of *groups* may not exceed the system-defined maximum "
"number of effective group ids, typically 16. See the documentation for "
":func:`getgroups` for cases where it may not return the same group list set "
"by calling setgroups()."
msgstr ""
"Na macOS, delka *groups* nesmusi prekrocit systemove-definovany maximalni "
"pocet efektivnich id skupin, typicky 16. Podivejte se na dokumentaci pro "
":func:`getgroups` pro pripady, kde nemuze vratit stejny seznam skupin "
"nastavenych volanim setgroups()."

#: ../../library/os.rst:636
msgid ""
"Reassociate the current thread with a Linux namespace. See the "
":manpage:`setns(2)` and :manpage:`namespaces(7)` man pages for more details."
msgstr ""
"Presouvej aktualne vlakno s Linux namespace. Podivejte se na "
":manpage:`setns(2)` a :manpage:`namespaces(7)` man stranky pro vice detailu."

#: ../../library/os.rst:640
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"If *fd* refers to a :file:`/proc/{pid}/ns/` link, ``setns()`` reassociates "
"the calling thread with the namespace associated with that link, and "
"*nstype* may be set to one of the :ref:`CLONE_NEW* constants <os-unshare-"
"clone-flags>` to impose constraints on the operation (``0`` means no "
"constraints)."
msgstr ""
"Pokud se *fd* vztahuje na odkaz :file:`/proc/{pid}/ns/`, ``setns()`` znovu "
"spoji volajici vlakno s namespace spojeny s tim odkazem, a *nstype* muze byt"
" nastaven na jednu z :ref:`CLONE_NEW* konstant <os-unshare-clone-flags>` pro"
" uvaleni omezenich na operaci (``0`` znamena zadna omezeni)."

#: ../../library/os.rst:647
msgid ""
"Since Linux 5.8, *fd* may refer to a PID file descriptor obtained from "
":func:`~os.pidfd_open`. In this case, ``setns()`` reassociates the calling "
"thread into one or more of the same namespaces as the thread referred to by "
"*fd*. This is subject to any constraints imposed by *nstype*, which is a bit"
" mask combining one or more of the :ref:`CLONE_NEW* constants <os-unshare-"
"clone-flags>`, e.g. ``setns(fd, os.CLONE_NEWUTS | os.CLONE_NEWPID)``. The "
"caller's memberships in unspecified namespaces are left unchanged."
msgstr ""
"Od Linuxu 5.8, *fd* muze odkazovat na deskriptor souboru PID ziskany z "
":func:`~os.pidfd_open`. V tomto pripade ``setns()`` znovu spoji volajici "
"vlakno do jedne nebo vice stejne namespaces jako vlakno odkazovane *fd*. "
"Toto je podrobeno jakymkoliv omezenihm uvaleneymi *nstype*, ktera je bitova "
"maska kombinujici jednu nebo vice z :ref:`CLONE_NEW* konstant <os-unshare-"
"clone-flags>`, npr ``setns(fd, os.CLONE_NEWUTS | os.CLONE_NEWPID)``. "
"Clenstvi volajiciho v neurcenych namespaces je ponechano beze zmene."

#: ../../library/os.rst:656
msgid ""
"*fd* can be any object with a :meth:`~io.IOBase.fileno` method, or a raw "
"file descriptor."
msgstr ""
"*fd* muze byt jakykoli objekt s metodou :meth:`~io.IOBase.fileno` nebo "
"surovy deskriptor souboru."

#: ../../library/os.rst:658
msgid ""
"This example reassociates the thread with the ``init`` process's network "
"namespace::"
msgstr ""
"Tento priklad znovu spoji vlakno s ``init`` proces network namespace::"

#: ../../library/os.rst:660
msgid ""
"fd = os.open(\"/proc/1/ns/net\", os.O_RDONLY)\n"
"os.setns(fd, os.CLONE_NEWNET)\n"
"os.close(fd)"
msgstr ""
"fd = os.open(\\\"/proc/1/ns/net\\\", os.O_RDONLY)\n"
"os.setns(fd, os.CLONE_NEWNET)\n"
"os.close(fd)"

#: ../../library/os.rst:670
msgid "The :func:`~os.unshare` function."
msgstr "Funkce :func:`~os.unshare`."

#: ../../library/os.rst:674
msgid ""
"Call the system call :c:func:`!setpgrp` or ``setpgrp(0, 0)`` depending on "
"which version is implemented (if any).  See the Unix manual for the "
"semantics."
msgstr ""
"Volej systemovy kall :c:func:`!setpgrp` nebo ``setpgrp(0, 0)`` podle toho, "
"ktere verzi je implementovana (pokud existuje). Podivejte se do Unix manualu"
" pro semantiku."

#: ../../library/os.rst:682
msgid ""
"Call the system call :c:func:`!setpgid` to set the process group id of the "
"process with id *pid* to the process group with id *pgrp*.  See the Unix "
"manual for the semantics."
msgstr ""
"Volej systemovy kall :c:func:`!setpgid` pro nastaveni id skupiny procesu "
"procesu s id *pid* na skupinu procesu s id *pgrp*. Podivejte se do Unix "
"manualu pro semantiku."

#: ../../library/os.rst:693
msgid ""
"Set program scheduling priority. The value *which* is one of "
":const:`PRIO_PROCESS`, :const:`PRIO_PGRP`, or :const:`PRIO_USER`, and *who* "
"is interpreted relative to *which* (a process identifier for "
":const:`PRIO_PROCESS`, process group identifier for :const:`PRIO_PGRP`, and "
"a user ID for :const:`PRIO_USER`). A zero value for *who* denotes "
"(respectively) the calling process, the process group of the calling "
"process, or the real user ID of the calling process. *priority* is a value "
"in the range -20 to 19. The default priority is 0; lower priorities cause "
"more favorable scheduling."
msgstr ""
"Nastav prioritu planovani programu. Hodnota *which* je jedna z "
":const:`PRIO_PROCESS`, :const:`PRIO_PGRP` nebo :const:`PRIO_USER` a *who* je"
" interpretovana vzhledem k *which* (identifikator procesu pro "
":const:`PRIO_PROCESS`, identifikator skupiny procesu pro :const:`PRIO_PGRP` "
"a uzivatelske id pro :const:`PRIO_USER`). Nulova hodnota pro *who* znaci "
"(respektive) volajici proces, skupinu procesu volajiciho procesu nebo "
"skutecne id uzivatele volajiciho procesu. *priority* je hodnota v rozsahu "
"-20 az 19. Vychozi priorita je 0; nizsi priority zpusobuji vice prychlenejsi"
" planovani."

#: ../../library/os.rst:710
msgid "Set the current process's real and effective group ids."
msgstr "Nastav skutecne a efektivni id skupiny aktualniho procesu."

#: ../../library/os.rst:717
msgid "Set the current process's real, effective, and saved group ids."
msgstr "Nastav skutecne, efektivni a ulozene id skupiny aktualniho procesu."

#: ../../library/os.rst:726
msgid "Set the current process's real, effective, and saved user ids."
msgstr "Nastav skutecne, efektivni a ulozene id uzivatele aktualniho procesu."

#: ../../library/os.rst:735
msgid "Set the current process's real and effective user ids."
msgstr "Nastav skutecne a efektivni id uzivatele aktualniho procesu."

#: ../../library/os.rst:742
msgid ""
"Call the system call :c:func:`!getsid`.  See the Unix manual for the "
"semantics."
msgstr ""
"Volej systemovy kall :c:func:`!getsid`. Podivejte se do Unix manualu pro "
"semantiku."

#: ../../library/os.rst:749
msgid ""
"Call the system call :c:func:`!setsid`.  See the Unix manual for the "
"semantics."
msgstr ""
"Volej systemovy kall :c:func:`!setsid`. Podivejte se do Unix manualu pro "
"semantiku."

#: ../../library/os.rst:758
msgid "Set the current process's user id."
msgstr "Nastav id uzivatele aktualniho procesu."

#: ../../library/os.rst:766
msgid ""
"Return the error message corresponding to the error code in *code*. On "
"platforms where :c:func:`!strerror` returns ``NULL`` when given an unknown "
"error number, :exc:`ValueError` is raised."
msgstr ""
"Vrati chybovou zpravu, ktera odpovida kodu chyby v *code*. Na platformach, "
"kde :c:func:`!strerror` vrati ``NULL`` kdyz je zadano neznamy kod chyby, je "
"vyvolvana :exc:`ValueError`."

#: ../../library/os.rst:773
msgid ""
"``True`` if the native OS type of the environment is bytes (eg. ``False`` on"
" Windows)."
msgstr ""
"``True`` pokud je nativni typ OS prostredi bajty (napr. ``False`` na "
"Windows)."

#: ../../library/os.rst:781
msgid "Set the current numeric umask and return the previous umask."
msgstr "Nastav aktualniho numerickeho umask a vrati predchozi umask."

#: ../../library/os.rst:793
msgid ""
"Returns information identifying the current operating system. The return "
"value is an object with five attributes:"
msgstr ""
"Vraci informace identifikujici aktualni operacni system. Navratova hodnota "
"je objekt s peti atributy:"

#: ../../library/os.rst:796
msgid ":attr:`sysname` - operating system name"
msgstr ":attr:`sysname` - nazev operacniho systemu"

#: ../../library/os.rst:797
msgid ":attr:`nodename` - name of machine on network (implementation-defined)"
msgstr ":attr:`nodename` - jmeno stroje v siti (zavisle na implementaci)"

#: ../../library/os.rst:798
msgid ":attr:`release` - operating system release"
msgstr ":attr:`release` - vydani operacniho systemu"

#: ../../library/os.rst:799
msgid ":attr:`version` - operating system version"
msgstr ":attr:`version` - verze operacniho systemu"

#: ../../library/os.rst:800
msgid ":attr:`machine` - hardware identifier"
msgstr ":attr:`machine` - identifikator hardwaru"

#: ../../library/os.rst:802
msgid ""
"For backwards compatibility, this object is also iterable, behaving like a "
"five-tuple containing :attr:`sysname`, :attr:`nodename`, :attr:`release`, "
":attr:`version`, and :attr:`machine` in that order."
msgstr ""
"Pro zpetnou kompatibilnost, tento objekt je taky iterovatelny, chovajici se "
"jako petituplice obsahujici :attr:`sysname`, :attr:`nodename`, "
":attr:`release`, :attr:`version` a :attr:`machine` v tomto poradi."

#: ../../library/os.rst:807
msgid ""
"Some systems truncate :attr:`nodename` to 8 characters or to the leading "
"component; a better way to get the hostname is :func:`socket.gethostname`  "
"or even ``socket.gethostbyaddr(socket.gethostname())``."
msgstr ""
"Nektere systemy zkracuji :attr:`nodename` na 8 znaku nebo na vedouci "
"komponentu; lepsi zpusob, jak ziskat jmeno pocitace je "
":func:`socket.gethostname` nebo jeste "
"``socket.gethostbyaddr(socket.gethostname())``."

#: ../../library/os.rst:812
msgid ""
"On macOS, iOS and Android, this returns the *kernel* name and version (i.e.,"
" ``'Darwin'`` on macOS and iOS; ``'Linux'`` on Android). "
":func:`platform.uname` can be used to get the user-facing operating system "
"name and version on iOS and Android."
msgstr ""
"Na macOS, iOS a Android, toto vrati *kernel* jmeno a verzi (tj ``'Darwin'`` "
"na macOS a iOS; ``'Linux'`` na Android). :func:`platform.uname` muze byt "
"pouzito pro ziskani uzivatelske-vzorove operacniho systemu jmena a verze na "
"iOS a Android."

#: ../../library/os.rst:819 ../../library/os.rst:5087
msgid ""
"Return type changed from a tuple to a tuple-like object with named "
"attributes."
msgstr ""
"Typ navratove hodnoty se zmenil z tuple na tuple-podobny objekt s "
"pojmenovavymi atributy."

#: ../../library/os.rst:828
msgid ""
"Unset (delete) the environment variable named *key*. Such changes to the "
"environment affect subprocesses started with :func:`os.system`, "
":func:`popen` or :func:`fork` and :func:`execv`."
msgstr ""
"Rusit (smazat) promenne prostredi pojmenovane *key*. Takove zmeny prostredi "
"ovlivnuji podprocesy spustene s :func:`os.system`, :func:`popen` nebo "
":func:`fork` a :func:`execv`."

#: ../../library/os.rst:832
msgid ""
"Deletion of items in :data:`os.environ` is automatically translated into a "
"corresponding call to :func:`unsetenv`; however, calls to :func:`unsetenv` "
"don't update :data:`os.environ`, so it is actually preferable to delete "
"items of :data:`os.environ`."
msgstr ""
"Smazani polozek v :data:`os.environ` je automaticky prevedeno na odpovidas "
"jici volan :func:`unsetenv`; nicmene volan :func:`unsetenv` nemeni "
":data:`os.environ`, takze je vlastne lepsi smazat polozky "
":data:`os.environ`."

#: ../../library/os.rst:839
msgid ""
"Raises an :ref:`auditing event <auditing>` ``os.unsetenv`` with argument "
"``key``."
msgstr ""
"Vyvola :ref:`auditni udalost <auditing>` ``os.unsetenv`` s argumentem "
"``key``."

#: ../../library/os.rst:841
msgid "The function is now always available and is also available on Windows."
msgstr "Funkce je nyn vzdy dostupna a je taky dostupna na Windows."

#: ../../library/os.rst:847
msgid ""
"Disassociate parts of the process execution context, and move them into a "
"newly created namespace. See the :manpage:`unshare(2)` man page for more "
"details. The *flags* argument is a bit mask, combining zero or more of the "
":ref:`CLONE_* constants <os-unshare-clone-flags>`, that specifies which "
"parts of the execution context should be unshared from their existing "
"associations and moved to a new namespace. If the *flags* argument is ``0``,"
" no changes are made to the calling process's execution context."
msgstr ""
"Odpoji casti kontextu spusteni procesu a presunout je do nove vytvore "
"namespace. Podivejte se na :manpage:`unshare(2)` stranku manualu pro vice "
"detailu. Argument *flags* je bitova maska, kombinujici nula nebo vice z "
":ref:`CLONE_* konstant <os-unshare-clone-flags>`, ktera specifikuje, ktere "
"casti kontextu spusteni by mely byt odpojeny od jejich existujicich "
"sdruzenil a presunout do nove namespace. Pokud je argument *flags* ``0``, "
"jsou zadne zmeny provedeny v kontextu spusteni volajiciho procesu."

#: ../../library/os.rst:864
msgid "The :func:`~os.setns` function."
msgstr "Funkce :func:`~os.setns`."

#: ../../library/os.rst:868
msgid ""
"Flags to the :func:`unshare` function, if the implementation supports them. "
"See :manpage:`unshare(2)` in the Linux manual for their exact effect and "
"availability."
msgstr ""
"Priznaky pro funkci :func:`unshare`, pokud implementace je podporuje. "
"Podivejte se na :manpage:`unshare(2)` v Linuxem manualu pro jejich presne "
"efekty a dostupnost."

#: ../../library/os.rst:891
msgid "File Object Creation"
msgstr "Vytvoreni objektu souboru"

#: ../../library/os.rst:893
msgid ""
"These functions create new :term:`file objects <file object>`.  (See also "
":func:`~os.open` for opening file descriptors.)"
msgstr ""
"Tyto funkce vytvarejii nove :term:`objekty souboru <file object>`. (Viz taky"
" :func:`~os.open` pro otevreji deskriptory souboru.)"

#: ../../library/os.rst:899
msgid ""
"Return an open file object connected to the file descriptor *fd*.  This is "
"an alias of the :func:`open` built-in function and accepts the same "
"arguments. The only difference is that the first argument of :func:`fdopen` "
"must always be an integer."
msgstr ""
"Vraci otevreii objekt souboru pripojeny na deskriptor souboru *fd*. Toto je "
"alias na vstavene funkce :func:`open` a prijima stejne argumenty. Jedina "
"rozdil je, ze prvni argument :func:`fdopen` musi vzdy byt cele cislo."

#: ../../library/os.rst:908
msgid "File Descriptor Operations"
msgstr "Operace deskriptoru souboru"

#: ../../library/os.rst:910
msgid ""
"These functions operate on I/O streams referenced using file descriptors."
msgstr ""
"Tyto funkce operuji na I/O streamech odkazovanych pouzivajici deskriptory "
"souboru."

#: ../../library/os.rst:912
msgid ""
"File descriptors are small integers corresponding to a file that has been "
"opened by the current process.  For example, standard input is usually file "
"descriptor 0, standard output is 1, and standard error is 2.  Further files "
"opened by a process will then be assigned 3, 4, 5, and so forth.  The name "
"\"file descriptor\" is slightly deceptive; on Unix platforms, sockets and "
"pipes are also referenced by file descriptors."
msgstr ""
"Deskriptory souboru jsou mala cisla odpovidas ejici souboru, ktery byl "
"otvoren aktualnim procesem. Napriklaid, standardni vstup je obvykle "
"deskriptor souboru 0, standardni vystup je 1 a standardni chyba je 2. Dalsi "
"soubory otevrene procesem budou pak prirazeny 3, 4, 5 a tak dal. Jmeno "
"\"deskriptor souboru\" je trochu klames ne; na Unix platformach jsou sockety"
" a roury taky odkazovany deskriptory souboru."

#: ../../library/os.rst:919
msgid ""
"The :meth:`~io.IOBase.fileno` method can be used to obtain the file "
"descriptor associated with a :term:`file object` when required.  Note that "
"using the file descriptor directly will bypass the file object methods, "
"ignoring aspects such as internal buffering of data."
msgstr ""
"Metoda :meth:`~io.IOBase.fileno` muze byt pouzita pro ziskani deskriptoru "
"souboru souvisejiciho s :term:`objektem souboru` kdyz je potreba. Vezmetev "
"na vedomí, ze pouziti deskriptoru souboru primo bude obejit metody objektu "
"souboru, ignorujici aspekty jako vnitrni cachovani dat."

#: ../../library/os.rst:927
msgid "Close file descriptor *fd*."
msgstr "Zavri deskriptor souboru *fd*."

#: ../../library/os.rst:931
msgid ""
"This function is intended for low-level I/O and must be applied to a file "
"descriptor as returned by :func:`os.open` or :func:`pipe`.  To close a "
"\"file object\" returned by the built-in function :func:`open` or by "
":func:`popen` or :func:`fdopen`, use its :meth:`~io.IOBase.close` method."
msgstr ""
"Tato funkce je urcena pro niz kokourovnove I/O a musi byt aplikovana na "
"deskriptor souboru jak je vraceno :func:`os.open` nebo :func:`pipe`. Pro "
"zavren \"objektu souboru\" vracenym vstaveny funkcemi :func:`open` nebo "
":func:`popen` nebo :func:`fdopen`, pouzijte jeho metodu "
":meth:`~io.IOBase.close`."

#: ../../library/os.rst:939
msgid ""
"Close all file descriptors from *fd_low* (inclusive) to *fd_high* "
"(exclusive), ignoring errors. Equivalent to (but much faster than)::"
msgstr ""
"Zavri vsechny deskriptory souboru z *fd_low* (vcetne) do *fd_high* "
"(vylucne), ignorujici chyby. Ekvivalentni (ale mnohem rychlejsi nez)::"

#: ../../library/os.rst:942
msgid ""
"for fd in range(fd_low, fd_high):\n"
"    try:\n"
"        os.close(fd)\n"
"    except OSError:\n"
"        pass"
msgstr ""
"for fd in range(fd_low, fd_high):\n"
"    try:\n"
"        os.close(fd)\n"
"    except OSError:\n"
"        pass"

#: ../../library/os.rst:951
msgid ""
"Copy *count* bytes from file descriptor *src*, starting from offset "
"*offset_src*, to file descriptor *dst*, starting from offset *offset_dst*. "
"If *offset_src* is ``None``, then *src* is read from the current position; "
"respectively for *offset_dst*."
msgstr ""
"Kopiruj *count* bajtu z deskriptoru souboru *src*, zacinjici od offsetu "
"*offset_src*, do deskriptoru souboru *dst*, zacinjici od offsetu "
"*offset_dst*. Pokud je *offset_src* ``None``, pak je *src* procitan z "
"aktualniho postaveni; respektive pro *offset_dst*."

#: ../../library/os.rst:956
msgid ""
"In Linux kernel older than 5.3, the files pointed to by *src* and *dst* must"
" reside in the same filesystem, otherwise an :exc:`OSError` is raised with "
":attr:`~OSError.errno` set to :const:`errno.EXDEV`."
msgstr ""
"V Linuxu jader starsi nez 5.3, soubory odkazovane *src* a *dst* musi byt "
"usidleny v stejnem systému souboru, jinak je vyvolvana :exc:`OSError` s "
":attr:`~OSError.errno` nastavenym na :const:`errno.EXDEV`."

#: ../../library/os.rst:960
msgid ""
"This copy is done without the additional cost of transferring data from the "
"kernel to user space and then back into the kernel. Additionally, some "
"filesystems could implement extra optimizations, such as the use of reflinks"
" (i.e., two or more inodes that share pointers to the same copy-on-write "
"disk blocks; supported file systems include btrfs and XFS) and server-side "
"copy (in the case of NFS)."
msgstr ""
"Tato kopie je provedem bez dodatecnych nakladu presunu dat z jad erne na "
"uzivatelsky prostor a pak zpet do jadra. Navic, nektere systémy souboru by "
"mohly implementovat extra optimalizace, jako je pouziti reflinks (tj dvou "
"nebo vice inode, ktere sdileji ukazatele na stejne copy-on-write diskove "
"bloky; podporovane systémy souboru zahrnuji btrfs a XFS) a server-side kopie"
" (v pripade NFS)."

#: ../../library/os.rst:967
msgid ""
"The function copies bytes between two file descriptors. Text options, like "
"the encoding and the line ending, are ignored."
msgstr ""
"Funkce kopiruje bajty mezi dvema deskriptory souboru. Moznosti textu, jako "
"je kodovani a konec radku, jsou ignorovany."

#: ../../library/os.rst:970
msgid ""
"The return value is the amount of bytes copied. This could be less than the "
"amount requested."
msgstr ""
"Navratova hodnota je mnozstvi skopirovanetch bajtu. Toto by mohlo byt mene "
"nez mnozstvi pozadovane."

#: ../../library/os.rst:975
msgid ""
"On Linux, :func:`os.copy_file_range` should not be used for copying a range "
"of a pseudo file from a special filesystem like procfs and sysfs. It will "
"always copy no bytes and return 0 as if the file was empty because of a "
"known Linux kernel issue."
msgstr ""
"Na Linuxu, :func:`os.copy_file_range` by nemela byt pouzivana pro "
"kopirovanichotovit rozsah pseudo-souboru ze specialniho systému souboru jako"
" procfs a sysfs. Vzdy bude kopirovat zadne bajty a vratit 0 jako by byl "
"soubor prazdny z duvodu zname Linux jaderne problemu."

#: ../../library/os.rst:987
msgid ""
"Return a string describing the encoding of the device associated with *fd* "
"if it is connected to a terminal; else return :const:`None`."
msgstr ""
"Vraci retezec popisujici kodovani zarize spojene s *fd* pokud je pripojena k"
" terminalu; jinak vraci :const:`None`."

#: ../../library/os.rst:990
msgid ""
"On Unix, if the :ref:`Python UTF-8 Mode <utf8-mode>` is enabled, return "
"``'UTF-8'`` rather than the device encoding."
msgstr ""
"Na Unixu, pokud je :ref:`Python UTF-8 Mode <utf8-mode>` povolen, vraci "
"``'UTF-8'`` miste kodovani zarize."

#: ../../library/os.rst:993
msgid "On Unix, the function now implements the Python UTF-8 Mode."
msgstr "Na Unixu, funkce nyn implementuje Python UTF-8 Mode."

#: ../../library/os.rst:999
msgid ""
"Return a duplicate of file descriptor *fd*. The new file descriptor is "
":ref:`non-inheritable <fd_inheritance>`."
msgstr ""
"Vraci duplikat deskriptoru souboru *fd*. Novy deskriptor souboru je "
":ref:`nelze dedicat <fd_inheritance>`."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1002
msgid ""
"On Windows, when duplicating a standard stream (0: stdin, 1: stdout, 2: "
"stderr), the new file descriptor is :ref:`inheritable <fd_inheritance>`."
msgstr ""
"Na Windows, kdyz duplikujes standardni stream (0: stdin, 1: stdout, 2: "
"stderr), novy deskriptor souboru je :ref:`dedicitelny <fd_inheritance>`."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1008 ../../library/os.rst:1293
msgid "The new file descriptor is now non-inheritable."
msgstr "Novy deskriptor souboru je nyn ne-dedicitelny."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1014
msgid ""
"Duplicate file descriptor *fd* to *fd2*, closing the latter first if "
"necessary. Return *fd2*. The new file descriptor is :ref:`inheritable "
"<fd_inheritance>` by default or non-inheritable if *inheritable* is "
"``False``."
msgstr ""
"Duplikuj deskriptor souboru *fd* na *fd2*, zavren vtsinu prvni pokud je "
"treba. Vraci *fd2*. Novy deskriptor souboru je :ref:`dedicitelny "
"<fd_inheritance>` ve vychozim stavu nebo ne-dedicitlelny pokud je "
"*inheritable* ``False``."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1021
msgid "Add the optional *inheritable* parameter."
msgstr "Pridej volitelny parametr *inheritable*."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1024
msgid "Return *fd2* on success. Previously, ``None`` was always returned."
msgstr "Vraci *fd2* pri uspechu. Drive vzdy byla vracena ``None``."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1030
msgid ""
"Change the mode of the file given by *fd* to the numeric *mode*.  See the "
"docs for :func:`chmod` for possible values of *mode*.  As of Python 3.3, "
"this is equivalent to ``os.chmod(fd, mode)``."
msgstr ""
"Zmeni rezhim souboru daneho *fd* na numericke *mode*. Podivejte se do docs "
"pro :func:`chmod` pro mozne hodnoty *mode*. Od Pythonu 3.3, toto je "
"ekvivalentni s ``os.chmod(fd, mode)``."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1034 ../../library/os.rst:2210
#: ../../library/os.rst:2311
msgid ""
"Raises an :ref:`auditing event <auditing>` ``os.chmod`` with arguments "
"``path``, ``mode``, ``dir_fd``."
msgstr ""
"Vyvola :ref:`auditni udalost <auditing>` ``os.chmod`` s argumenty ``path``, "
"``mode``, ``dir_fd``."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1038 ../../library/os.rst:1056
#: ../../library/os.rst:1147 ../../library/os.rst:1759
#: ../../library/os.rst:2207 ../../library/os.rst:2240
#: ../../library/os.rst:3536
msgid ""
"The function is limited on WASI, see :ref:`wasm-availability` for more "
"information."
msgstr ""
"Funkce je omezena na WASI, viz :ref:`wasm-availability` pro vice informaci."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1041 ../../library/os.rst:2318
msgid "Added support on Windows."
msgstr "Pridana podpora na Windows."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1047
msgid ""
"Change the owner and group id of the file given by *fd* to the numeric *uid*"
" and *gid*.  To leave one of the ids unchanged, set it to -1.  See "
":func:`chown`.  As of Python 3.3, this is equivalent to ``os.chown(fd, uid, "
"gid)``."
msgstr ""
"Zmeni vlastnika a id skupiny souboru daneho *fd* na numericke *uid* a *gid*."
" Pro opusteni jednoho z ids beze zmene, nastav ho na -1. Viz :func:`chown`. "
"Od Pythonu 3.3, toto je ekvivalentni s ``os.chown(fd, uid, gid)``."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1052 ../../library/os.rst:2236
#: ../../library/os.rst:2327
msgid ""
"Raises an :ref:`auditing event <auditing>` ``os.chown`` with arguments "
"``path``, ``uid``, ``gid``, ``dir_fd``."
msgstr ""
"Vyvola :ref:`auditni udalost <auditing>` ``os.chown`` s argumenty ``path``, "
"``uid``, ``gid``, ``dir_fd``."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1062
msgid ""
"Force write of file with filedescriptor *fd* to disk. Does not force update "
"of metadata."
msgstr ""
"Vynutit zapis souboru s deskriptorem souboru *fd* na disk. Nevynucuje "
"aktualizaci metadat."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1068
msgid "This function is not available on MacOS."
msgstr "Tato funkce neni dostupna na MacOS."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1073
msgid ""
"Return system configuration information relevant to an open file. *name* "
"specifies the configuration value to retrieve; it may be a string which is "
"the name of a defined system value; these names are specified in a number of"
" standards (POSIX.1, Unix 95, Unix 98, and others).  Some platforms define "
"additional names as well.  The names known to the host operating system are "
"given in the ``pathconf_names`` dictionary.  For configuration variables not"
" included in that mapping, passing an integer for *name* is also accepted."
msgstr ""
"Vraci informace o konfiguraci systemu relevantni k otevrenemu souboru. "
"*name* specifikuje konfiguracni hodnotu k ziskani; muze to byt retezec, "
"ktery je jmeno definovane sistemove hodnoty; tato jmena jsou specifikovana v"
" mnozstvi standartu (POSIX.1, Unix 95, Unix 98 a ostatni). Nektere platformy"
" definuji dodatecna jmena jako dobre. Jmena znama hostovskemu operačnímu "
"systému jsou dana v slovniku ``pathconf_names``. Pro konfiguracni promenne "
"neobsazene v tomto mapovani, prideleni celehocisl pro *name* je taky "
"prijimanem."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1081 ../../library/os.rst:2647
msgid ""
"If *name* is a string and is not known, :exc:`ValueError` is raised.  If a "
"specific value for *name* is not supported by the host system, even if it is"
" included in ``pathconf_names``, an :exc:`OSError` is raised with "
":const:`errno.EINVAL` for the error number."
msgstr ""
"Pokud je *name* retezec a neni znam, je vyvolvana :exc:`ValueError`. Pokud "
"specifikova hodnota pro *name* neni podporovana hostovskem systému, i kdyby "
"byla zahrnuta v ``pathconf_names``, je vyvolvana :exc:`OSError` s "
":const:`errno.EINVAL` pro cislo chyby."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1086
msgid "As of Python 3.3, this is equivalent to ``os.pathconf(fd, name)``."
msgstr "Od Pythonu 3.3, toto je ekvivalentni s ``os.pathconf(fd, name)``."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1093
msgid ""
"Get the status of the file descriptor *fd*. Return a :class:`stat_result` "
"object."
msgstr ""
"Ziskej status deskriptoru souboru *fd*. Vraci :class:`stat_result` objekt."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1096
msgid "As of Python 3.3, this is equivalent to ``os.stat(fd)``."
msgstr "Od Pythonu 3.3, toto je ekvivalentni s ``os.stat(fd)``."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1100 ../../library/os.rst:2475
msgid "The :func:`.stat` function."
msgstr "Funkce :func:`.stat`."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1105
msgid ""
"Return information about the filesystem containing the file associated with "
"file descriptor *fd*, like :func:`statvfs`.  As of Python 3.3, this is "
"equivalent to ``os.statvfs(fd)``."
msgstr ""
"Vraci informace o systému souboru obsahujici soubor spojeny s deskriptorem "
"souboru *fd*, jako :func:`statvfs`. Od Pythonu 3.3, toto je ekvivalentni s "
"``os.statvfs(fd)``."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1114
msgid ""
"Force write of file with filedescriptor *fd* to disk.  On Unix, this calls "
"the native :c:func:`!fsync` function; on Windows, the MS :c:func:`!_commit` "
"function."
msgstr ""
"Vynutit zapis souboru s deskriptorem souboru *fd* na disk. Na Unixu, toto "
"vola nativni funkce :c:func:`!fsync`; na Windows, MS :c:func:`!_commit` "
"funkce."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1117
msgid ""
"If you're starting with a buffered Python :term:`file object` *f*, first do "
"``f.flush()``, and then do ``os.fsync(f.fileno())``, to ensure that all "
"internal buffers associated with *f* are written to disk."
msgstr ""
"Pokud zacinates s vyrovnavaci Python :term:`objektem souboru` *f*, prvni "
"provest ``f.flush()``, a pak provest ``os.fsync(f.fileno())``, aby se "
"zajistilo, ze vsechny vnitrni vyrovnavace spojene s *f* jsou napsany na "
"disk."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1126
msgid ""
"Truncate the file corresponding to file descriptor *fd*, so that it is at "
"most *length* bytes in size.  As of Python 3.3, this is equivalent to "
"``os.truncate(fd, length)``."
msgstr ""
"Zkrati soubor odpovidas ejici deskriptoru souboru *fd*, tak aby byl nejvyse "
"*length* bajtu ve velikosti. Od Pythonu 3.3, toto je ekvivalentni s "
"``os.truncate(fd, length)``."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1130
msgid ""
"Raises an :ref:`auditing event <auditing>` ``os.truncate`` with arguments "
"``fd``, ``length``."
msgstr ""
"Vyvola :ref:`auditni udalost <auditing>` ``os.truncate`` s argumenty ``fd``,"
" ``length``."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1134 ../../library/os.rst:3575
msgid "Added support for Windows"
msgstr "Pridana podpora pro Windows"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1140
msgid ""
"Get the blocking mode of the file descriptor: ``False`` if the "
":data:`O_NONBLOCK` flag is set, ``True`` if the flag is cleared."
msgstr ""
"Ziskej blokujici rezhim deskriptoru souboru: ``False`` pokud je nastaven "
":data:`O_NONBLOCK` prrapor, ``True`` pokud je prrapor vymazan."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1143
msgid "See also :func:`set_blocking` and :meth:`socket.socket.setblocking`."
msgstr "Viz taky :func:`set_blocking` a :meth:`socket.socket.setblocking`."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1150 ../../library/os.rst:1762
msgid "On Windows, this function is limited to pipes."
msgstr "Na Windows, tato funkce je omezena na roury."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1154 ../../library/os.rst:1766
msgid "Added support for pipes on Windows."
msgstr "Pridana podpora pro roury na Windows."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1160
msgid ""
"Grant access to the slave pseudo-terminal device associated with the master "
"pseudo-terminal device to which the file descriptor *fd* refers. The file "
"descriptor *fd* is not closed upon failure."
msgstr ""
"Poskytnout pristup k pseudo-terminalove zarizeni otoku souvisejicimu s "
"pseudo-terminalovym zarizenim hlavy, na ktere se deskriptor souboru *fd* "
"vztahuje. Deskriptor souboru *fd* neni zavreny pri selhani."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1164
msgid "Calls the C standard library function :c:func:`grantpt`."
msgstr "Vola funkci C standardni knihovny :c:func:`grantpt`."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1173
msgid ""
"Return ``True`` if the file descriptor *fd* is open and connected to a "
"tty(-like) device, else ``False``."
msgstr ""
"Vraci ``True`` pokud je deskriptor souboru *fd* otvoren a pripojena k "
"tty(-podobne) zarizeni, jinak ``False``."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1179
msgid ""
"Apply, test or remove a POSIX lock on an open file descriptor. *fd* is an "
"open file descriptor. *cmd* specifies the command to use - one of "
":data:`F_LOCK`, :data:`F_TLOCK`, :data:`F_ULOCK` or :data:`F_TEST`. *len* "
"specifies the section of the file to lock."
msgstr ""
"Aplikuj, testuj nebo odstrante POSIX zamek na otevreny deskriptor souboru. "
"*fd* je otvoren deskriptor souboru. *cmd* specifikuje prikaz k pouziti - "
"jeden z :data:`F_LOCK`, :data:`F_TLOCK`, :data:`F_ULOCK` nebo "
":data:`F_TEST`. *len* specifikuje sekci souboru k zamceni."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1185
msgid ""
"Raises an :ref:`auditing event <auditing>` ``os.lockf`` with arguments "
"``fd``, ``cmd``, ``len``."
msgstr ""
"Vyvola :ref:`auditni udalost <auditing>` ``os.lockf`` s argumenty ``fd``, "
"``cmd``, ``len``."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1197
msgid "Flags that specify what action :func:`lockf` will take."
msgstr "Priznaky, ktere specifikuji, co by :func:`lockf` provedlo."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1206
msgid ""
"Prepare the tty of which fd is a file descriptor for a new login session. "
"Make the calling process a session leader; make the tty the controlling tty,"
" the stdin, the stdout, and the stderr of the calling process; close fd."
msgstr ""
"Priprav tty, ktery je fd deskriptor souboru, na novou prihlasovaci relaci. "
"Cini volajici proces vedouci relace; cini tty kontrolujici tty, stdin, "
"stdout a stderr volajiciho procesu; zavri fd."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1217
msgid ""
"Set the current position of file descriptor *fd* to position *pos*, modified"
" by *whence*, and return the new position in bytes relative to the start of "
"the file. Valid values for *whence* are:"
msgstr ""
"Nastav aktualni pozici deskriptoru souboru *fd* na pozici *pos*, upravena "
"*whence*, a vraci novou pozici v bajtech vzhledem k zacatku souboru. Platne "
"hodnoty pro *whence* jsou:"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1222
msgid ""
":const:`SEEK_SET` or ``0`` -- set *pos* relative to the beginning of the "
"file"
msgstr ""
":const:`SEEK_SET` nebo ``0`` -- nastav *pos* vzhledem k zacatku souboru"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1223
msgid ""
":const:`SEEK_CUR` or ``1`` -- set *pos* relative to the current file "
"position"
msgstr ""
":const:`SEEK_CUR` nebo ``1`` -- nastav *pos* vzhledem k aktualni pozici "
"souboru"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1224
msgid ""
":const:`SEEK_END` or ``2`` -- set *pos* relative to the end of the file"
msgstr ":const:`SEEK_END` nebo ``2`` -- nastav *pos* vzhledem k konci souboru"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1225
msgid ""
":const:`SEEK_HOLE` -- set *pos* to the next data location, relative to *pos*"
msgstr ""
":const:`SEEK_HOLE` -- nastav *pos* na dalsi umisteni dat, vzhledem k *pos*"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1226
msgid ""
":const:`SEEK_DATA` -- set *pos* to the next data hole, relative to *pos*"
msgstr ""
":const:`SEEK_DATA` -- nastav *pos* na dalsi diru v datech, vzhledem k *pos*"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1230
msgid "Add support for :const:`!SEEK_HOLE` and :const:`!SEEK_DATA`."
msgstr "Pridej podporu pro :const:`!SEEK_HOLE` a :const:`!SEEK_DATA`."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1237
msgid ""
"Parameters to the :func:`lseek` function and the :meth:`~io.IOBase.seek` "
"method on :term:`file-like objects <file object>`, for whence to adjust the "
"file position indicator."
msgstr ""
"Parametry pro funkci :func:`lseek` a metodu :meth:`~io.IOBase.seek` na "
":term:`objektech podobne souboru <file object>`, pro whence k upraveni "
"pozice indikandu souboru."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1241
msgid ":const:`SEEK_SET`"
msgstr ":const:`SEEK_SET`"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1242
msgid "Adjust the file position relative to the beginning of the file."
msgstr "Upravit pozici souboru vzhledem k zacatku souboru."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1243
msgid ":const:`SEEK_CUR`"
msgstr ":const:`SEEK_CUR`"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1244
msgid "Adjust the file position relative to the current file position."
msgstr "Upravit pozici souboru vzhledem k aktualni pozici souboru."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1245
msgid ":const:`SEEK_END`"
msgstr ":const:`SEEK_END`"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1246
msgid "Adjust the file position relative to the end of the file."
msgstr "Upravit pozici souboru vzhledem k konci souboru."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1248
msgid "Their values are 0, 1, and 2, respectively."
msgstr "Jejich hodnoty jsou 0, 1 a 2, respektive."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1254
msgid ""
"Parameters to the :func:`lseek` function and the :meth:`~io.IOBase.seek` "
"method on :term:`file-like objects <file object>`, for seeking file data and"
" holes on sparsely allocated files."
msgstr ""
"Parametry pro funkci :func:`lseek` a metodu :meth:`~io.IOBase.seek` na "
":term:`objektech podobne souboru <file object>`, pro hledani dat a der v "
"souboru sparývatych souboru."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1258
msgid ":data:`!SEEK_DATA`"
msgstr ":data:`!SEEK_DATA`"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1259
msgid ""
"Adjust the file offset to the next location containing data, relative to the"
" seek position."
msgstr ""
"Upravit offset souboru na dalsi umisteni obsahujici data, vzhledem k pozici "
"hledani."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1262
msgid ":data:`!SEEK_HOLE`"
msgstr ":data:`!SEEK_HOLE`"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1263
msgid ""
"Adjust the file offset to the next location containing a hole, relative to "
"the seek position. A hole is defined as a sequence of zeros."
msgstr ""
"Upravit offset souboru na dalsi umisteni obsahujici diru, vzhledem k pozici "
"hledani. Dira je definovana jako sekvence nul."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1269
msgid "These operations only make sense for filesystems that support them."
msgstr ""
"Tyto operace maji smysl pouze pro systémy souboru, ktere je podporuji."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1278
msgid ""
"Open the file *path* and set various flags according to *flags* and possibly"
" its mode according to *mode*.  When computing *mode*, the current umask "
"value is first masked out.  Return the file descriptor for the newly opened "
"file. The new file descriptor is :ref:`non-inheritable <fd_inheritance>`."
msgstr ""
"Otevri soubor *path* a nastav ruzne driveny podle *flags* a mozna jeho "
"rezhim podle *mode*. Pri vypoctu *mode*, je prvni hodnota aktualni umask "
"maskova. Vraci deskriptor souboru pro nove otvoren soubor. Novy deskriptor "
"souboru je :ref:`ne-dedicitelny <fd_inheritance>`."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1283
msgid ""
"For a description of the flag and mode values, see the C run-time "
"documentation; flag constants (like :const:`O_RDONLY` and :const:`O_WRONLY`)"
" are defined in the :mod:`os` module.  In particular, on Windows adding "
":const:`O_BINARY` is needed to open files in binary mode."
msgstr ""
"Pro popis praporu a rezhimu hodnot, viz C runtime dokumentaci; konstanty "
"praporu (jako :const:`O_RDONLY` a :const:`O_WRONLY`) jsou definovany v "
"modulu :mod:`os`. Zejme, na Windows pridavani :const:`O_BINARY` je potreba "
"pro otevren souboru v binarnim rezhimu."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1288
msgid ""
"This function can support :ref:`paths relative to directory descriptors "
"<dir_fd>` with the *dir_fd* parameter."
msgstr ""
"Tato funkce muze podporovat :ref:`cesty relativni k deskriptorum adresare "
"<dir_fd>` s parametrem *dir_fd*."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1291
msgid ""
"Raises an :ref:`auditing event <auditing>` ``open`` with arguments ``path``,"
" ``mode``, ``flags``."
msgstr ""
"Vyvola :ref:`auditni udalost <auditing>` ``open`` s argumenty ``path``, "
"``mode``, ``flags``."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1298
msgid ""
"This function is intended for low-level I/O.  For normal usage, use the "
"built-in function :func:`open`, which returns a :term:`file object` with "
":meth:`~file.read` and :meth:`~file.write` methods (and many more).  To wrap"
" a file descriptor in a file object, use :func:`fdopen`."
msgstr ""
"Tato funkce je urcena pro niz kokourovnove I/O. Pro normalnih uziti, "
"pouzijte vstavene funkce :func:`open`, ktera vraci :term:`objektem souboru` "
"s metodami :meth:`~file.read` a :meth:`~file.write` (a mnohem vice). Pro "
"zabaleni deskriptoru souboru v objektu souboru, pouzijte :func:`fdopen`."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1303 ../../library/os.rst:2480
#: ../../library/os.rst:2520 ../../library/os.rst:2591
#: ../../library/os.rst:2613 ../../library/os.rst:2694
#: ../../library/os.rst:2724 ../../library/os.rst:2831
#: ../../library/os.rst:3591
msgid "Added the *dir_fd* parameter."
msgstr "Pridan parametr *dir_fd*."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1306 ../../library/os.rst:1657
#: ../../library/os.rst:1892 ../../library/os.rst:5183
msgid ""
"If the system call is interrupted and the signal handler does not raise an "
"exception, the function now retries the system call instead of raising an "
":exc:`InterruptedError` exception (see :pep:`475` for the rationale)."
msgstr ""
"Pokud je systemovy prikaz prerusen a obsluhovac signalu nevyvolava vyjimku, "
"funkce nyn opakuje systemovy prikaz miste vyvolan :exc:`InterruptedError` "
"vyjimky (viz :pep:`475` pro oduvodneni)."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1311 ../../library/os.rst:2103
#: ../../library/os.rst:2135 ../../library/os.rst:2166
#: ../../library/os.rst:2216 ../../library/os.rst:2257
#: ../../library/os.rst:2297 ../../library/os.rst:2315
#: ../../library/os.rst:2331 ../../library/os.rst:2391
#: ../../library/os.rst:2483 ../../library/os.rst:2523
#: ../../library/os.rst:2567 ../../library/os.rst:2594
#: ../../library/os.rst:2616 ../../library/os.rst:2657
#: ../../library/os.rst:2727 ../../library/os.rst:2746
#: ../../library/os.rst:2834 ../../library/os.rst:3124
#: ../../library/os.rst:3411 ../../library/os.rst:3578
#: ../../library/os.rst:3594 ../../library/os.rst:3634
#: ../../library/os.rst:3734 ../../library/os.rst:3795
#: ../../library/os.rst:4192 ../../library/os.rst:4372
#: ../../library/os.rst:4941
msgid "Accepts a :term:`path-like object`."
msgstr "Prijima :term:`cestu podobnou objektu`."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1314
msgid ""
"The following constants are options for the *flags* parameter to the "
":func:`~os.open` function.  They can be combined using the bitwise OR "
"operator ``|``.  Some of them are not available on all platforms.  For "
"descriptions of their availability and use, consult the :manpage:`open(2)` "
"manual page on Unix or `the MSDN <https://msdn.microsoft.com/en-"
"us/library/z0kc8e3z.aspx>`_ on Windows."
msgstr ""
"Nasledujici konstanty jsou moznosti pro parametr *flags* k funkci "
":func:`~os.open`. Mohou byt kombinovany pouzitim bitoveho operatoru OR "
"``|``. Nektere z nich nejsou dostupne na vsech platformach. Pro popisy "
"jejich dostupnosti a pouziti, konzultujte :manpage:`open(2)` stranku manualu"
" na Unixu nebo `MSDN <https://msdn.microsoft.com/en-"
"us/library/z0kc8e3z.aspx>`_ na Windows."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1329
msgid "The above constants are available on Unix and Windows."
msgstr "Vyse uvedene konstanty jsou dostupne na Unixu a Windows."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1340
msgid "The above constants are only available on Unix."
msgstr "Vyse uvedene konstanty jsou dostupne pouze na Unixu."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1342
msgid "Add :data:`O_CLOEXEC` constant."
msgstr "Pridej :data:`O_CLOEXEC` konstantu."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1353
msgid "The above constants are only available on Windows."
msgstr "Vyse uvedene konstanty jsou dostupne pouze na Windows."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1360
msgid "The above constants are only available on macOS."
msgstr "Vyse uvedene konstanty jsou dostupne pouze na macOS."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1362
msgid ""
"Add :data:`O_EVTONLY`, :data:`O_FSYNC`, :data:`O_SYMLINK` and "
":data:`O_NOFOLLOW_ANY` constants."
msgstr ""
"Pridej :data:`O_EVTONLY`, :data:`O_FSYNC`, :data:`O_SYMLINK` a "
":data:`O_NOFOLLOW_ANY` konstanty."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1376
msgid ""
"The above constants are extensions and not present if they are not defined "
"by the C library."
msgstr ""
"Vyse uvedene konstanty jsou rozsireni a nejsou pritomny pokud nejsou "
"definovany knihovnou C."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1379
msgid ""
"Add :data:`O_PATH` on systems that support it. Add :data:`O_TMPFILE`, only "
"available on Linux Kernel 3.11   or newer."
msgstr ""
"Pridej :data:`O_PATH` v systemech, ktere je podporuji. Pridej "
":data:`O_TMPFILE`, dostupne pouze na Linux Kernel 3.11 nebo novejsi."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1389
msgid ""
"Open a new pseudo-terminal pair. Return a pair of file descriptors "
"``(master, slave)`` for the pty and the tty, respectively. The new file "
"descriptors are :ref:`non-inheritable <fd_inheritance>`. For a (slightly) "
"more portable approach, use the :mod:`pty` module."
msgstr ""
"Otevri novy par pseudo-terminalu. Vrati par deskriptoru souboru ``(master, "
"slave)`` pro pty a tty, respektive. Nove deskriptory souboru jsou :ref:`ne-"
"dedicitelne <fd_inheritance>`. Pro (trochu) prenositelneji pristu, pouzijte "
"modul :mod:`pty`."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1396 ../../library/os.rst:1408
msgid "The new file descriptors are now non-inheritable."
msgstr "Nove deskriptory souboru jsou nyn ne-dedicitelne."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1402
msgid ""
"Create a pipe.  Return a pair of file descriptors ``(r, w)`` usable for "
"reading and writing, respectively. The new file descriptor is :ref:`non-"
"inheritable <fd_inheritance>`."
msgstr ""
"Vytvor rouru. Vraci par deskriptoru souboru ``(r, w)`` pouzitelne pro cteni "
"a psani, respektive. Novy deskriptor souboru je :ref:`ne-dedicitelny "
"<fd_inheritance>`."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1414
msgid ""
"Create a pipe with *flags* set atomically. *flags* can be constructed by "
"ORing together one or more of these values: :data:`O_NONBLOCK`, "
":data:`O_CLOEXEC`. Return a pair of file descriptors ``(r, w)`` usable for "
"reading and writing, respectively."
msgstr ""
"Vytvor rouru s *flags* nastaveny atomicky. *flags* mohou byt vystaveny "
"kombinovanjem jedne nebo vice z techto hodnot: :data:`O_NONBLOCK`, "
":data:`O_CLOEXEC`. Vraci par deskriptoru souboru ``(r, w)`` pouzitelne pro "
"cteni a psani, respektive."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1427
msgid ""
"Ensures that enough disk space is allocated for the file specified by *fd* "
"starting from *offset* and continuing for *len* bytes."
msgstr ""
"Zajisti, ze je dostatek diskoveho prostoru vyhrazeno pro soubor "
"specifikovany *fd* zacinjici od *offset* a pokracujici pro *len* bajtu."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1437
msgid ""
"Announces an intention to access data in a specific pattern thus allowing "
"the kernel to make optimizations. The advice applies to the region of the "
"file specified by *fd* starting at *offset* and continuing for *len* bytes. "
"*advice* is one of :data:`POSIX_FADV_NORMAL`, :data:`POSIX_FADV_SEQUENTIAL`,"
" :data:`POSIX_FADV_RANDOM`, :data:`POSIX_FADV_NOREUSE`, "
":data:`POSIX_FADV_WILLNEED` or :data:`POSIX_FADV_DONTNEED`."
msgstr ""
"Hlase namer pristup k datum v specifickemu vzoru umoznenujici jadru provest "
"optimalizace. Rada se vztahuje na oblast souboru specifikovana *fd* "
"zacinjici v *offset* a pokracujici pro *len* bajtu. *advice* je jeden z "
":data:`POSIX_FADV_NORMAL`, :data:`POSIX_FADV_SEQUENTIAL`, "
":data:`POSIX_FADV_RANDOM`, :data:`POSIX_FADV_NOREUSE`, "
":data:`POSIX_FADV_WILLNEED` nebo :data:`POSIX_FADV_DONTNEED`."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1457
msgid ""
"Flags that can be used in *advice* in :func:`posix_fadvise` that specify the"
" access pattern that is likely to be used."
msgstr ""
"Priznaky, ktere mohou byt pouzity v *advice* v :func:`posix_fadvise`, ktere "
"specifikuji vzor pristupu, ktery bude pouzit."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1467
msgid ""
"Read at most *n* bytes from file descriptor *fd* at a position of *offset*, "
"leaving the file offset unchanged."
msgstr ""
"Precti nejvyse *n* bajtu z deskriptoru souboru *fd* na pozici *offset*, "
"opoustedajici offset souboru beze zmeny."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1470 ../../library/os.rst:1646
msgid ""
"Return a bytestring containing the bytes read. If the end of the file "
"referred to by *fd* has been reached, an empty bytes object is returned."
msgstr ""
"Vraci retezec bajtu obsahujici precten bajty. Pokud byl dosazenim konce "
"souboru odkazovaneho *fd*, je vracen prazdny objekt bajtu."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1480
msgid "Open and return a file descriptor for a master pseudo-terminal device."
msgstr ""
"Otevri a vrati deskriptor souboru pro master pseudo-terminale zarizeni."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1482
msgid ""
"Calls the C standard library function :c:func:`posix_openpt`. The *oflag* "
"argument is used to set file status flags and file access modes as specified"
" in the manual page of :c:func:`posix_openpt` of your system."
msgstr ""
"Vola funkci C standardni knihovny :c:func:`posix_openpt`. Argument *oflag* "
"je pouzit k nastaveni priznaku stavu souboru a rezhimu pristupu souboru jak "
"je specifikovano na stranku manualu :c:func:`posix_openpt` vaseho systemu."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1486
msgid ""
"The returned file descriptor is :ref:`non-inheritable <fd_inheritance>`. If "
"the value :data:`O_CLOEXEC` is available on the system, it is added to "
"*oflag*."
msgstr ""
"Vraceny deskriptor souboru je :ref:`ne-dedicitelny <fd_inheritance>`. Pokud "
"je hodnota :data:`O_CLOEXEC` dostupna na systemu, je pridana na *oflag*."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1497
msgid ""
"Read from a file descriptor *fd* at a position of *offset* into mutable "
":term:`bytes-like objects <bytes-like object>` *buffers*, leaving the file "
"offset unchanged.  Transfer data into each buffer until it is full and then "
"move on to the next buffer in the sequence to hold the rest of the data."
msgstr ""
"Precti z deskriptoru souboru *fd* na pozici *offset* do mutabilniho "
":term:`bajt-podobne objektu <bytes-like object>` *buffers*, opoustedajici "
"offset souboru beze zmeny. Prenesere data do kazdeho vyrovnavace az dokud "
"neni plny a pak prejit na dalsi vyrovnavac v sekvenci pro uchyceni zbytku "
"dat."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1502 ../../library/os.rst:1587
msgid ""
"The flags argument contains a bitwise OR of zero or more of the following "
"flags:"
msgstr ""
"Argument flags obsahuje bitovy OR nula nebo vice z nasledujicich priznaku:"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1505
msgid ":data:`RWF_HIPRI`"
msgstr ":data:`RWF_HIPRI`"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1506
msgid ":data:`RWF_NOWAIT`"
msgstr ":data:`RWF_NOWAIT`"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1508 ../../library/os.rst:1829
msgid ""
"Return the total number of bytes actually read which can be less than the "
"total capacity of all the objects."
msgstr ""
"Vraci celkovy pocet bajtu skutecne prectene, ktere mohou byt mene nez "
"celkova kapacita vsech objektu."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1511 ../../library/os.rst:1596
#: ../../library/os.rst:1832 ../../library/os.rst:1907
msgid ""
"The operating system may set a limit (:func:`sysconf` value "
"``'SC_IOV_MAX'``) on the number of buffers that can be used."
msgstr ""
"Operacni system muze nastavit limit (:func:`sysconf` hodnota "
"``'SC_IOV_MAX'``) na pocet vyrovnavcu, ktere mohou byt pouzity."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1514
msgid "Combine the functionality of :func:`os.readv` and :func:`os.pread`."
msgstr "Kombinuj funkcnost :func:`os.readv` a :func:`os.pread`."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1518 ../../library/os.rst:1603
msgid "Using flags requires Linux >= 4.6."
msgstr "Pouziti flags vyzaduje Linux >= 4.6."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1525
msgid ""
"Do not wait for data which is not immediately available. If this flag is "
"specified, the system call will return instantly if it would have to read "
"data from the backing storage or wait for a lock."
msgstr ""
"Necekej na data, ktere neni okamzite dostupna. Pokud je tento prrapor "
"specifikovany, systemovy prikaz vraci okamzite, pokud by musel cist data z "
"uloziste nebo cekat na zamek."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1529
msgid ""
"If some data was successfully read, it will return the number of bytes read."
" If no bytes were read, it will return ``-1`` and set errno to "
":const:`errno.EAGAIN`."
msgstr ""
"Pokud byla nektere data uspesne prectena, vraci pocet prectench bajtu. Pokud"
" bylo precteno zadne bajty, vraci ``-1`` a nastavuje errno na "
":const:`errno.EAGAIN`."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1540
msgid ""
"High priority read/write. Allows block-based filesystems to use polling of "
"the device, which provides lower latency, but may use additional resources."
msgstr ""
"Cteni/zapis s vysokou prioritou. Umoznje blok-bazovane systémy souboru "
"pouzit dotazovani zarizeni, ktere poskytuje nizi latenci, ale muze pouzit "
"dodatecne zdroje."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1544
msgid ""
"Currently, on Linux, this feature is usable only on a file descriptor opened"
" using the :data:`O_DIRECT` flag."
msgstr ""
"V soucasnosti na Linuxu, tato funkce je pouzitelna pouze na deskriptoru "
"souboru otvorenem pouzitim :data:`O_DIRECT` praporu."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1554
msgid ""
"Return the name of the slave pseudo-terminal device associated with the "
"master pseudo-terminal device to which the file descriptor *fd* refers. The "
"file descriptor *fd* is not closed upon failure."
msgstr ""
"Vraci jmeno slave pseudo-terminale zarizeni souvisejiciho s master pseudo-"
"terminalovym zarizenim, na ktere se deskriptor souboru *fd* vztahuje. "
"Deskriptor souboru *fd* neni zavreny pri selhani."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1558
msgid ""
"Calls the reentrant C standard library function :c:func:`ptsname_r` if it is"
" available; otherwise, the C standard library function :c:func:`ptsname`, "
"which is not guaranteed to be thread-safe, is called."
msgstr ""
"Vola reentrant C standardni knihovny funkce :c:func:`ptsname_r` pokud je "
"dostupna; jinak, C standardni knihovny funkce :c:func:`ptsname`, ktera neni "
"zarucenarova jako vlakno-bezpecna, je volana."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1569
msgid ""
"Write the bytestring in *str* to file descriptor *fd* at position of "
"*offset*, leaving the file offset unchanged."
msgstr ""
"Napis retezec bajtu v *str* do deskriptoru souboru *fd* na pozici *offset*, "
"opoustedajici offset souboru beze zmeny."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1572 ../../library/os.rst:1882
msgid "Return the number of bytes actually written."
msgstr "Vraci pocet bajtu skutecne napsanych."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1581
msgid ""
"Write the *buffers* contents to file descriptor *fd* at an offset *offset*, "
"leaving the file offset unchanged.  *buffers* must be a sequence of "
":term:`bytes-like objects <bytes-like object>`. Buffers are processed in "
"array order. Entire contents of the first buffer is written before "
"proceeding to the second, and so on."
msgstr ""
"Napis obsah *buffers* do deskriptoru souboru *fd* v offsetu *offset*, "
"opoustedajici offset souboru beze zmeny. *buffers* musi byt sekvence "
":term:`bajt-podobne objektu <bytes-like object>`. Vyrovnavace jsou "
"zpracovany v poradi pole. Cely obsah prvniho vyrovnavace je napsanpred tim, "
"nez se prejde k druhemu a tak dal."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1590
msgid ":data:`RWF_DSYNC`"
msgstr ":data:`RWF_DSYNC`"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1591
msgid ":data:`RWF_SYNC`"
msgstr ":data:`RWF_SYNC`"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1592
msgid ":data:`RWF_APPEND`"
msgstr ":data:`RWF_APPEND`"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1594
msgid "Return the total number of bytes actually written."
msgstr "Vraci celkovy pocet bajtu skutecne napsanych."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1599
msgid "Combine the functionality of :func:`os.writev` and :func:`os.pwrite`."
msgstr "Kombinuj funkcnost :func:`os.writev` a :func:`os.pwrite`."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1610
msgid ""
"Provide a per-write equivalent of the :data:`O_DSYNC` :func:`os.open` flag. "
"This flag effect applies only to the data range written by the system call."
msgstr ""
"Poskytnout za-zapis ekvivalent :data:`O_DSYNC` :func:`os.open` praporu. "
"Efekt tohoto praporu se vztahuje pouze na rozsah dat napsany systemovym "
"prikazem."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1620
msgid ""
"Provide a per-write equivalent of the :data:`O_SYNC` :func:`os.open` flag. "
"This flag effect applies only to the data range written by the system call."
msgstr ""
"Poskytnout za-zapis ekvivalent :data:`O_SYNC` :func:`os.open` praporu. Efekt"
" tohoto praporu se vztahuje pouze na rozsah dat napsany systemovym prikazem."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1630
msgid ""
"Provide a per-write equivalent of the :data:`O_APPEND` :func:`os.open` flag."
" This flag is meaningful only for :func:`os.pwritev`, and its effect applies"
" only to the data range written by the system call. The *offset* argument "
"does not affect the write operation; the data is always appended to the end "
"of the file. However, if the *offset* argument is ``-1``, the current file "
"*offset* is updated."
msgstr ""
"Poskytnout za-zapis ekvivalent :data:`O_APPEND` :func:`os.open` praporu. "
"Tento prrapor je vyznamny pouze pro :func:`os.pwritev` a jeho efekt se "
"vztahuje pouze na rozsah dat napsany systemovym prikazem. Argument *offset* "
"neovlivnuje operaci zapis; data jsou vzdy pripojena na konci souboru. "
"Nicmene, pokud je argument *offset* ``-1``, je aktualizovan *offset* "
"aktualni souboru."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1644
msgid "Read at most *n* bytes from file descriptor *fd*."
msgstr "Precti nejvyse *n* bajtu z deskriptoru souboru *fd*."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1651
msgid ""
"This function is intended for low-level I/O and must be applied to a file "
"descriptor as returned by :func:`os.open` or :func:`pipe`.  To read a \"file"
" object\" returned by the built-in function :func:`open` or by :func:`popen`"
" or :func:`fdopen`, or :data:`sys.stdin`, use its :meth:`~file.read` or "
":meth:`~file.readline` methods."
msgstr ""
"Tato funkce je urcena pro niz kokourovnove I/O a musi byt aplikovana na "
"deskriptor souboru jak je vraceno :func:`os.open` nebo :func:`pipe`. Pro "
"cteni \"objektu souboru\" vracenym vstaveny funkcemi :func:`open` nebo "
":func:`popen` nebo :func:`fdopen` nebo :data:`sys.stdin`, pouzijte jeho "
":meth:`~file.read` nebo :meth:`~file.readline` metody."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1665
msgid ""
"Read from a file descriptor *fd* into a mutable :ref:`buffer object "
"<bufferobjects>` *buffer*."
msgstr ""
"Precti z deskriptoru souboru *fd* do mutabilniho :ref:`objektu vyrovnavace "
"<bufferobjects>` *buffer*."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1668
msgid ""
"The *buffer* should be mutable and :term:`bytes-like <bytes-like object>`. "
"On success, returns the number of bytes read. Less bytes may be read than "
"the size of the buffer. The underlying system call will be retried when "
"interrupted by a signal, unless the signal handler raises an exception. "
"Other errors will not be retried and an error will be raised."
msgstr ""
"*buffer* by mel byt mutabilni a :term:`bajt-podobny <bytes-like object>`. "
"Pri uspechu, vraci pocet prectench bajtu. Mene bajtu muze byt precteno nez "
"velikost vyrovnavace. Podkladovy systemovy prikaz bude znovu pokusen kdy je "
"prerusen signaler, pokud obsluhovac signalu nevyvolava vyjimku. Ostatni "
"chyby nebudou opakovany a chyba bude vyvolvana."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1674
msgid ""
"Returns 0 if *fd* is at end of file or if the provided *buffer* has length 0"
" (which can be used to check for errors without reading data). Never returns"
" negative."
msgstr ""
"Vraci 0 pokud je *fd* na konci souboru nebo pokud je poskytnuty *buffer* "
"delky 0 (ktery muze byt pouzit pro kontrolu chyb bez cteni dat). Nikdy "
"nevrati negativni."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1680
msgid ""
"This function is intended for low-level I/O and must be applied to a file "
"descriptor as returned by :func:`os.open` or :func:`os.pipe`.  To read a "
"\"file object\" returned by the built-in function :func:`open`, or "
":data:`sys.stdin`, use its member functions, for example "
":meth:`io.BufferedIOBase.readinto`, :meth:`io.BufferedIOBase.read`, or "
":meth:`io.TextIOBase.read`"
msgstr ""
"Tato funkce je urcena pro niz kokourovnove I/O a musi byt aplikovana na "
"deskriptor souboru jak je vraceno :func:`os.open` nebo :func:`os.pipe`. Pro "
"cteni \"objektu souboru\" vracenym vstaveny funkcemi :func:`open` nebo "
":data:`sys.stdin`, pouzijte jeho clenske funkce, napriklaid "
":meth:`io.BufferedIOBase.readinto`, :meth:`io.BufferedIOBase.read` nebo "
":meth:`io.TextIOBase.read`"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1693
msgid ""
"Copy *count* bytes from file descriptor *in_fd* to file descriptor *out_fd* "
"starting at *offset*. Return the number of bytes sent. When EOF is reached "
"return ``0``."
msgstr ""
"Kopiruj *count* bajtu z deskriptoru souboru *in_fd* do deskriptoru souboru "
"*out_fd* zacinjici v *offset*. Vraci pocet bajtu odeslanych. Kdyz je "
"dosazenim EOF vraci ``0``."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1697
msgid ""
"The first function notation is supported by all platforms that define "
":func:`sendfile`."
msgstr ""
"Prvni notace funkce je podporovana vsemi platformami, ktere definuji "
":func:`sendfile`."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1700
msgid ""
"On Linux, if *offset* is given as ``None``, the bytes are read from the "
"current position of *in_fd* and the position of *in_fd* is updated."
msgstr ""
"Na Linuxu, pokud je *offset* dany jako ``None``, jsou bajty precteny z "
"aktualni pozice *in_fd* a pozice *in_fd* je aktualizovana."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1703
msgid ""
"The second case may be used on macOS and FreeBSD where *headers* and "
"*trailers* are arbitrary sequences of buffers that are written before and "
"after the data from *in_fd* is written. It returns the same as the first "
"case."
msgstr ""
"Druhy pripad muze byt pouzit na macOS a FreeBSD kde *headers* a *trailers* "
"jsou libovolne sekvence vyrovnavcu, ktere jsou napsany pred a po datech z "
"*in_fd* je napsano. Vraci stejne jako prvni pripad."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1707
msgid ""
"On macOS and FreeBSD, a value of ``0`` for *count* specifies to send until "
"the end of *in_fd* is reached."
msgstr ""
"Na macOS a FreeBSD, hodnota ``0`` pro *count* specifikuje poslani az do "
"dosazeni konce *in_fd*."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1710
msgid ""
"All platforms support sockets as *out_fd* file descriptor, and some "
"platforms allow other types (e.g. regular file, pipe) as well."
msgstr ""
"Vsechny platformy podporuji sockety jako *out_fd* deskriptor souboru a "
"nektere platformy umozneji ostatni typy (napr. obycejny soubor, roura) jako "
"dobre."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1713
msgid ""
"Cross-platform applications should not use *headers*, *trailers* and *flags*"
" arguments."
msgstr ""
"Meziplatformni aplikace by nemely pouzivat argumenty *headers*, *trailers* a"
" *flags*."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1720
msgid ""
"For a higher-level wrapper of :func:`sendfile`, see "
":meth:`socket.socket.sendfile`."
msgstr ""
"Pro vyse-urovnovy obal :func:`sendfile`, viz :meth:`socket.socket.sendfile`."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1725
msgid "Parameters *out* and *in* was renamed to *out_fd* and *in_fd*."
msgstr "Parametry *out* a *in* byly prejmenovat na *out_fd* a *in_fd*."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1733
msgid ""
"Parameters to the :func:`sendfile` function, if the implementation supports "
"them."
msgstr ""
"Parametry pro funkci :func:`sendfile`, pokud implementace je podporuje."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1742
msgid ""
"Parameter to the :func:`sendfile` function, if the implementation supports "
"it. The data won't be cached in the virtual memory and will be freed "
"afterwards."
msgstr ""
"Parametr pro funkci :func:`sendfile`, pokud implementace je podporuje. Data "
"nebudou ulozena do virtualni pameti a budou osvobojena pozdeji."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1752
msgid ""
"Set the blocking mode of the specified file descriptor. Set the "
":data:`O_NONBLOCK` flag if blocking is ``False``, clear the flag otherwise."
msgstr ""
"Nastav blokujici rezhim specifikovaneho deskriptoru souboru. Nastav "
":data:`O_NONBLOCK` prrapor pokud je blocking ``False``, vymaz prrapor jinak."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1755
msgid "See also :func:`get_blocking` and :meth:`socket.socket.setblocking`."
msgstr "Viz taky :func:`get_blocking` a :meth:`socket.socket.setblocking`."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1772
msgid ""
"Transfer *count* bytes from file descriptor *src*, starting from offset "
"*offset_src*, to file descriptor *dst*, starting from offset *offset_dst*."
msgstr ""
"Prenesi *count* bajtu z deskriptoru souboru *src*, zacinjici od offsetu "
"*offset_src*, do deskriptoru souboru *dst*, zacinjici od offsetu "
"*offset_dst*."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1775
msgid ""
"The splicing behaviour can be modified by specifying a *flags* value. Any of"
" the following variables may used, combined using bitwise OR (the ``|`` "
"operator):"
msgstr ""
"Chování splicing muze byt zmeneé specifikaci *flags* hodnoty. Jakekoli z "
"nasledujicich promennych muze byt pouzita, kombinovana pouzitim bitoveho OR "
"(``|`` operator):"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1779
msgid ""
"If :const:`SPLICE_F_MOVE` is specified, the kernel is asked to move pages "
"instead of copying, but pages may still be copied if the kernel cannot move "
"the pages from the pipe."
msgstr ""
"Pokud je :const:`SPLICE_F_MOVE` specifikovany, je kernel pozadan pro presun "
"stranek miste kopirovani, ale stranky muze byt kopirovany pokud kernel "
"nemoze presunout stranky z roury."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1783
msgid ""
"If :const:`SPLICE_F_NONBLOCK` is specified, the kernel is asked to not block"
" on I/O. This makes the splice pipe operations nonblocking, but splice may "
"nevertheless block because the spliced file descriptors may block."
msgstr ""
"Pokud je :const:`SPLICE_F_NONBLOCK` specifikovany, je kernel pozadan k "
"neblokovani na I/O. Toto cinni splice roura operace neblokujici, ale splice "
"muze nicmene blokovat, protože spliced deskriptory souboru mohou blokovat."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1788
msgid ""
"If :const:`SPLICE_F_MORE` is specified, it hints to the kernel that more "
"data will be coming in a subsequent splice."
msgstr ""
"Pokud je :const:`SPLICE_F_MORE` specifikovany, jsou to napoveda pro kernel, "
"ze bude prichazet vic dat v nasledujici splice."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1791
msgid ""
"At least one of the file descriptors must refer to a pipe. If *offset_src* "
"is ``None``, then *src* is read from the current position; respectively for "
"*offset_dst*. The offset associated to the file descriptor that refers to a "
"pipe must be ``None``. The files pointed to by *src* and *dst* must reside "
"in the same filesystem, otherwise an :exc:`OSError` is raised with "
":attr:`~OSError.errno` set to :const:`errno.EXDEV`."
msgstr ""
"Nejmene jeden z deskriptoru souboru se musi vztahovat na rouru. Pokud je "
"*offset_src* ``None``, pak je *src* procitan z aktualniho postaveni; "
"respektive pro *offset_dst*. Offset spojeny s deskriptorem souboru, ktery se"
" vztahuje na rouru, musi byt ``None``. Soubory odkazovane *src* a *dst* musi"
" byt usidleny v stejnem systému souboru, jinak je vyvolvana :exc:`OSError` s"
" :attr:`~OSError.errno` nastavenym na :const:`errno.EXDEV`."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1798
msgid ""
"This copy is done without the additional cost of transferring data from the "
"kernel to user space and then back into the kernel. Additionally, some "
"filesystems could implement extra optimizations. The copy is done as if both"
" files are opened as binary."
msgstr ""
"Tato kopie je provedena bez dodatecnych nakladu presunu dat z jaderna do "
"uzivatelskebo prostoru a pak zpet do jaderna. Navic, nektere systémy souboru"
" by mohly implementovat extra optimalizace. Kopie je provedena jako by oba "
"soubory byli otevreny jako binarni."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1803
msgid ""
"Upon successful completion, returns the number of bytes spliced to or from "
"the pipe. A return value of 0 means end of input. If *src* refers to a pipe,"
" then this means that there was no data to transfer, and it would not make "
"sense to block because there are no writers connected to the write end of "
"the pipe."
msgstr ""
"Pri uspechu, vraci pocet bajtu spliced do nebo z roury. Navratova hodnota 0 "
"znamena konec vstupu. Pokud se *src* vztahuje na rouru, pak to znamena, ze "
"nebylo zadne data k prenosu a nely by to mit smysl blokovat protoze nejsou "
"zadni pisaci pripojeni k zapisu konce roury."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1809
msgid "The :manpage:`splice(2)` man page."
msgstr "Stranka :manpage:`splice(2)` manualu."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1824
msgid ""
"Read from a file descriptor *fd* into a number of mutable :term:`bytes-like "
"objects <bytes-like object>` *buffers*. Transfer data into each buffer until"
" it is full and then move on to the next buffer in the sequence to hold the "
"rest of the data."
msgstr ""
"Precti z deskriptoru souboru *fd* do poctu mutabilnich :term:`bajt-podobne "
"objektu <bytes-like object>` *buffers*. Prenesi data do kazdeho vyrovnavace "
"az dokud neni plny a pak prejit na dalsi vyrovnavac v sekvenci pro uchyceni "
"zbytku dat."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1842
msgid ""
"Return the process group associated with the terminal given by *fd* (an open"
" file descriptor as returned by :func:`os.open`)."
msgstr ""
"Vraci skupinu procesu spojenou s terminalem danym *fd* (otevreny deskriptor "
"souboru jak je vraceno :func:`os.open`)."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1850
msgid ""
"Set the process group associated with the terminal given by *fd* (an open "
"file descriptor as returned by :func:`os.open`) to *pg*."
msgstr ""
"Nastav skupinu procesu spojenou s terminalem danym *fd* (otevreny deskriptor"
" souboru jak je vraceno :func:`os.open`) na *pg*."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1858
msgid ""
"Return a string which specifies the terminal device associated with file "
"descriptor *fd*.  If *fd* is not associated with a terminal device, an "
"exception is raised."
msgstr ""
"Vraci retezec, ktery specifikuje terminale zarizeni spojene s deskriptorem "
"souboru *fd*. Pokud se *fd* nespojuje s terminalem zarizenim, je vyvolvana "
"vyjimka."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1867
msgid ""
"Unlock the slave pseudo-terminal device associated with the master pseudo-"
"terminal device to which the file descriptor *fd* refers. The file "
"descriptor *fd* is not closed upon failure."
msgstr ""
"Odemkni slave pseudo-terminale zarizeni spojene s master pseudo-terminalovym"
" zarizenim, na ktere se deskriptor souboru *fd* vztahuje. Deskriptor souboru"
" *fd* neni zavreny pri selhani."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1871
msgid "Calls the C standard library function :c:func:`unlockpt`."
msgstr "Vola C standardni knihovny funkce :c:func:`unlockpt`."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1880
msgid "Write the bytestring in *str* to file descriptor *fd*."
msgstr "Napis retezec bajtu v *str* do deskriptoru souboru *fd*."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1886
msgid ""
"This function is intended for low-level I/O and must be applied to a file "
"descriptor as returned by :func:`os.open` or :func:`pipe`.  To write a "
"\"file object\" returned by the built-in function :func:`open` or by "
":func:`popen` or :func:`fdopen`, or :data:`sys.stdout` or "
":data:`sys.stderr`, use its :meth:`~file.write` method."
msgstr ""
"Tato funkce je urcena pro niz kokourovnove I/O a musi byt aplikovana na "
"deskriptor souboru jak je vraceno :func:`os.open` nebo :func:`pipe`. Pro "
"psani \"objektu souboru\" vracenym vstaveny funkcemi :func:`open` nebo "
":func:`popen` nebo :func:`fdopen` nebo :data:`sys.stdout` nebo "
":data:`sys.stderr`, pouzijte jeho metodu :meth:`~file.write`."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1900
msgid ""
"Write the contents of *buffers* to file descriptor *fd*. *buffers* must be a"
" sequence of :term:`bytes-like objects <bytes-like object>`. Buffers are "
"processed in array order. Entire contents of the first buffer is written "
"before proceeding to the second, and so on."
msgstr ""
"Napis obsah *buffers* do deskriptoru souboru *fd*. *buffers* musi byt "
"sekvence :term:`bajt-podobne objektu <bytes-like object>`. Vyrovnavace jsou "
"zpracovany v poradi pole. Cely obsah prvniho vyrovnavace je napsanpred tim, "
"nez se prejde k druhemu a tak dal."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1905
msgid "Returns the total number of bytes actually written."
msgstr "Vraci celkovy pocet bajtu skutecne napsanych."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1918
msgid "Querying the size of a terminal"
msgstr "Dotazovani na velikost terminalu"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1924
msgid ""
"Return the size of the terminal window as ``(columns, lines)``, tuple of "
"type :class:`terminal_size`."
msgstr ""
"Vraci velikost okna terminalu jako ``(columns, lines)`` tuple typu "
":class:`terminal_size`."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1927
msgid ""
"The optional argument ``fd`` (default ``STDOUT_FILENO``, or standard output)"
" specifies which file descriptor should be queried."
msgstr ""
"Volitelny argument ``fd`` (vychozi ``STDOUT_FILENO`` nebo standardni vystup)"
" specifikuje, ktery deskriptor souboru by mel byt dotazan."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1930
msgid ""
"If the file descriptor is not connected to a terminal, an :exc:`OSError` is "
"raised."
msgstr ""
"Pokud se deskriptor souboru nespojuje s terminalem, je vyvolvana "
":exc:`OSError`."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1933
msgid ""
":func:`shutil.get_terminal_size` is the high-level function which should "
"normally be used, ``os.get_terminal_size`` is the low-level implementation."
msgstr ""
":func:`shutil.get_terminal_size` je vysoko-urovnova funkce, ktera by "
"normalne mela byt pouzita, ``os.get_terminal_size`` je niz kokourovnova "
"implementace."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1941
msgid ""
"A subclass of tuple, holding ``(columns, lines)`` of the terminal window "
"size."
msgstr ""
"Podtrida tuple, kterou se drzi ``(columns, lines)`` okna terminalu "
"velikosti."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1945
msgid "Width of the terminal window in characters."
msgstr "Sirka okna terminalu v znacich."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1949
msgid "Height of the terminal window in characters."
msgstr "Vyska okna terminalu v znacich."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1955
msgid "Inheritance of File Descriptors"
msgstr "Dedicnost deskriptoru souboru"

#: ../../library/os.rst:1959
msgid ""
"A file descriptor has an \"inheritable\" flag which indicates if the file "
"descriptor can be inherited by child processes.  Since Python 3.4, file "
"descriptors created by Python are non-inheritable by default."
msgstr ""
"Deskriptor souboru ma \"dedicitelny\" prrapor, ktery udava, zda se "
"deskriptor souboru muze dedicat na detske procesy. Od Pythonu 3.4, "
"deskriptory souboru vytvorene Pythonem jsou ne-dedicitelne ve vychozim "
"stavu."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1963
msgid ""
"On UNIX, non-inheritable file descriptors are closed in child processes at "
"the execution of a new program, other file descriptors are inherited. Note "
"that non-inheritable file descriptors are still *inherited* by child "
"processes on :func:`os.fork`."
msgstr ""
"Na UNIX, ne-dicitelne deskriptory souboru jsou zavreny v detskeych procesech"
" pri spusteni noveho programu, ostatni deskriptory souboru jsou dediceny. "
"Vezměte na vedomí, ze ne-dedicitelne deskriptory souboru jsou stale "
"*dediceny* na detske procesy na :func:`os.fork`."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1967
msgid ""
"On Windows, non-inheritable handles and file descriptors are closed in child"
" processes, except for standard streams (file descriptors 0, 1 and 2: stdin,"
" stdout and stderr), which are always inherited.  Using :func:`spawn\\* "
"<spawnl>` functions, all inheritable handles and all inheritable file "
"descriptors are inherited. Using the :mod:`subprocess` module, all file "
"descriptors except standard streams are closed, and inheritable handles are "
"only inherited if the *close_fds* parameter is ``False``."
msgstr ""
"Na Windows, ne-dedicitelne handle a deskriptory souboru jsou zavreny v "
"detskych procesech, krome standardnich streamu (deskriptory souboru 0, 1 a "
"2: stdin, stdout a stderr), ktere jsou vzdy dediceny. Pouziti "
":func:`spawn\\* <spawnl>` funkci, vsechny dedicitelne handle a vse "
"deskriptory souboru jsou dediceny. Pouziti modulu :mod:`subprocess`, vsechny"
" deskriptory souboru krome standardnich streamu jsou zavreny a dedicitelne "
"handle jsou dediceny pouze pokud je parametr *close_fds* ``False``."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1975
msgid "On WebAssembly platforms, the file descriptor cannot be modified."
msgstr "Na WebAssembly platformach, deskriptor souboru nemoze byt zmene."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1979
msgid "Get the \"inheritable\" flag of the specified file descriptor (a boolean)."
msgstr ""
"Ziskej \"dedicitelny\" prrapor specifikovaneho deskriptoru souboru "
"(boolean)."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1983
msgid "Set the \"inheritable\" flag of the specified file descriptor."
msgstr "Nastav \"dedicitelny\" prrapor specifikovaneho deskriptoru souboru."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1987
msgid "Get the \"inheritable\" flag of the specified handle (a boolean)."
msgstr "Ziskej \"dedicitelny\" prrapor specifikovaneho handle (boolean)."

#: ../../library/os.rst:1993
msgid "Set the \"inheritable\" flag of the specified handle."
msgstr "Nastav \"dedicitelny\" prrapor specifikovaneho handle."

#: ../../library/os.rst:2001
msgid "Files and Directories"
msgstr "Soubory a adresare"

#: ../../library/os.rst:2003
msgid ""
"On some Unix platforms, many of these functions support one or more of these"
" features:"
msgstr ""
"Na nektere Unix platformach, mnoheo z techto funkci podporuji jednu nebo "
"vice z techto vlastnosti:"

#: ../../library/os.rst:2008
msgid ""
"**specifying a file descriptor:** Normally the *path* argument provided to "
"functions in the :mod:`os` module must be a string specifying a file path.  "
"However, some functions now alternatively accept an open file descriptor for"
" their *path* argument. The function will then operate on the file referred "
"to by the descriptor. For POSIX systems, Python will call the variant of the"
" function prefixed with ``f`` (e.g. call ``fchdir`` instead of ``chdir``)."
msgstr ""
"**specifikace deskriptoru souboru:** Normalne argument *path* poskytnuty na "
"funkce v modulu :mod:`os` musi byt retezec specifikujici cestu souboru. "
"Nicmene, nektere funkce nyn alternativne prijimaji otevreny deskriptor "
"souboru pro jejich *path* argument. Funkce bude pak operovat na souboru "
"odkazovane deskriptorem. Pro POSIX systemy, Python bude volat variantu "
"funkce s priponou ``f`` (napr vola ``fchdir`` miste ``chdir``)."

#: ../../library/os.rst:2016
msgid ""
"You can check whether or not *path* can be specified as a file descriptor "
"for a particular function on your platform using :data:`os.supports_fd`. If "
"this functionality is unavailable, using it will raise a "
":exc:`NotImplementedError`."
msgstr ""
"Muzete zkontrolovat, zda *path* muze byt specifikovan jako deskriptor "
"souboru pro konkretni funkci na vasi platforme pouzitim "
":data:`os.supports_fd`. Pokud je tato funkcnost nedostupna, jeji pouziti "
"bude vyvolan :exc:`NotImplementedError`."

#: ../../library/os.rst:2021
msgid ""
"If the function also supports *dir_fd* or *follow_symlinks* arguments, it's "
"an error to specify one of those when supplying *path* as a file descriptor."
msgstr ""
"Pokud funkce take podporuje argumenty *dir_fd* nebo *follow_symlinks*, je "
"chybou specifikovat jeden z nich kdyz dodavate *path* jako deskriptor "
"souboru."

#: ../../library/os.rst:2026
msgid ""
"**paths relative to directory descriptors:** If *dir_fd* is not ``None``, it"
" should be a file descriptor referring to a directory, and the path to "
"operate on should be relative; path will then be relative to that directory."
"  If the path is absolute, *dir_fd* is ignored.  For POSIX systems, Python "
"will call the variant of the function with an ``at`` suffix and possibly "
"prefixed with ``f`` (e.g. call ``faccessat`` instead of ``access``)."
msgstr ""
"**cesty vztahujici se k adresaroveym deskriptorum:** Pokud *dir_fd* neni "
"``None``, mela by to byt deskriptor souboru odkazujici na adresare a cesta "
"na operaci by mela byt relativni; cesta bude pak relativni k tomuto "
"adresari. Pokud je cesta absolutni, *dir_fd* je ignorovana. Pro POSIX "
"systemy, Python bude volat variantu funkce s priponou ``at`` a mozna s "
"priponou ``f`` (napr vola ``faccessat`` miste ``access``)."

#: ../../library/os.rst:2033
msgid ""
"You can check whether or not *dir_fd* is supported for a particular function"
" on your platform using :data:`os.supports_dir_fd`.  If it's unavailable, "
"using it will raise a :exc:`NotImplementedError`."
msgstr ""
"Muzete zkontrolovat, zda *dir_fd* je podporovana pro konkretni funkci na "
"vasi platforme pouzitim :data:`os.supports_dir_fd`. Pokud je nedostupna, "
"jeji pouziti bude vyvolan :exc:`NotImplementedError`."

#: ../../library/os.rst:2039
msgid ""
"**not following symlinks:** If *follow_symlinks* is ``False``, and the last "
"element of the path to operate on is a symbolic link, the function will "
"operate on the symbolic link itself rather than the file pointed to by the "
"link.  For POSIX systems, Python will call the ``l...`` variant of the "
"function."
msgstr ""
"**nesledovani symlinku:** Pokud je *follow_symlinks* ``False`` a posledni "
"prvek cesty na operaci je symlink, funkce bude operovat na samotnem symlinku"
" miste souboru odkazovaneho odkazem. Pro POSIX systemy, Python bude volat "
"``l...`` variantu funkce."

#: ../../library/os.rst:2045
msgid ""
"You can check whether or not *follow_symlinks* is supported for a particular"
" function on your platform using :data:`os.supports_follow_symlinks`. If "
"it's unavailable, using it will raise a :exc:`NotImplementedError`."
msgstr ""
"Muzete zkontrolovat, zda *follow_symlinks* je podporovana pro konkretni "
"funkci na vasi platforme pouzitim :data:`os.supports_follow_symlinks`. Pokud"
" je nedostupna, jeji pouziti bude vyvolan :exc:`NotImplementedError`."

#: ../../library/os.rst:2053
msgid ""
"Use the real uid/gid to test for access to *path*.  Note that most "
"operations will use the effective uid/gid, therefore this routine can be "
"used in a suid/sgid environment to test if the invoking user has the "
"specified access to *path*.  *mode* should be :const:`F_OK` to test the "
"existence of *path*, or it can be the inclusive OR of one or more of "
":const:`R_OK`, :const:`W_OK`, and :const:`X_OK` to test permissions.  Return"
" :const:`True` if access is allowed, :const:`False` if not. See the Unix man"
" page :manpage:`access(2)` for more information."
msgstr ""
"Pouzij skutecne uid/gid k testovani pristupu na *path*. Vezmetev na vedomí, "
"ze vetsina operaci bude pouzivat efektivni uid/gid, proto tedy tato rutina "
"muze byt pouzita v suid/sgid prostredi k testovani, zda volan uzivatel ma "
"specifikovany pristup k *path*. *mode* by mely byt :const:`F_OK` k testovani"
" existence *path* nebo muze byt inklusivni OR jedne nebo vice z "
":const:`R_OK`, :const:`W_OK` a :const:`X_OK` k testovani oprávnění. Vrati "
":const:`True` pokud je pristup povolen, :const:`False` pokud neni. Podivejte"
" se do Unix manstranky :manpage:`access(2)` pro vice informaci."

#: ../../library/os.rst:2062
msgid ""
"This function can support specifying :ref:`paths relative to directory "
"descriptors <dir_fd>` and :ref:`not following symlinks <follow_symlinks>`."
msgstr ""
"Tato funkce muze podporovat specifikaci :ref:`cest vztahujici se k "
"adresaroveym deskriptorum <dir_fd>` a :ref:`nesledovani symlinku "
"<follow_symlinks>`."

#: ../../library/os.rst:2065
msgid ""
"If *effective_ids* is ``True``, :func:`access` will perform its access "
"checks using the effective uid/gid instead of the real uid/gid. "
"*effective_ids* may not be supported on your platform; you can check whether"
" or not it is available using :data:`os.supports_effective_ids`.  If it is "
"unavailable, using it will raise a :exc:`NotImplementedError`."
msgstr ""
"Pokud je *effective_ids* ``True``, :func:`access` provede své kontroly "
"pristupu pouzitim efektivniho uid/gid miste skutecneho uid/gid. "
"*effective_ids* nemuze byt podporovana na vasi platforme; muzete "
"zkontrolovat, zda je dostupna pouzitim :data:`os.supports_effective_ids`. "
"Pokud je nedostupna, jeji pouziti bude vyvolan :exc:`NotImplementedError`."

#: ../../library/os.rst:2073
msgid ""
"Using :func:`access` to check if a user is authorized to e.g. open a file "
"before actually doing so using :func:`open` creates a security hole, because"
" the user might exploit the short time interval between checking and opening"
" the file to manipulate it. It's preferable to use :term:`EAFP` techniques. "
"For example::"
msgstr ""
"Pouziti :func:`access` k kontrole, zda je uzivatel autorizovan na napr. "
"otevren soubor pred skutecnym ukonem pouzitim :func:`open` vyvoji "
"bezpecnostni chybu, protoze uzivatel muze vyuzit kratkouacasovy interval "
"mezi kontrolou a otevrenim souboru k jeho manipulaci. Je lepsi pouzit "
":term:`EAFP` techniky. Napriklaid::"

#: ../../library/os.rst:2079
msgid ""
"if os.access(\"myfile\", os.R_OK):\n"
"    with open(\"myfile\") as fp:\n"
"        return fp.read()\n"
"return \"some default data\""
msgstr ""
"if os.access(\"myfile\", os.R_OK):\n"
"    with open(\"myfile\") as fp:\n"
"        return fp.read()\n"
"return \"some default data\""

#: ../../library/os.rst:2084
msgid "is better written as::"
msgstr "je lepe napsano jako::"

#: ../../library/os.rst:2086
msgid ""
"try:\n"
"    fp = open(\"myfile\")\n"
"except PermissionError:\n"
"    return \"some default data\"\n"
"else:\n"
"    with fp:\n"
"        return fp.read()"
msgstr ""
"try:\n"
"    fp = open(\"myfile\")\n"
"except PermissionError:\n"
"    return \"some default data\"\n"
"else:\n"
"    with fp:\n"
"        return fp.read()"

#: ../../library/os.rst:2096
msgid ""
"I/O operations may fail even when :func:`access` indicates that they would "
"succeed, particularly for operations on network filesystems which may have "
"permissions semantics beyond the usual POSIX permission-bit model."
msgstr ""
"I/O operace mohou selhat, i kdyz :func:`access` udava, ze by byla uspesna, "
"zejme pro operace na sitovych systémech souboru, ktere mohou mit semantiku "
"oprávnění pres obycejny POSIX modelu opcniho bitu."

#: ../../library/os.rst:2100
msgid "Added the *dir_fd*, *effective_ids*, and *follow_symlinks* parameters."
msgstr "Pridany parametry *dir_fd*, *effective_ids* a *follow_symlinks*."

#: ../../library/os.rst:2112
msgid ""
"Values to pass as the *mode* parameter of :func:`access` to test the "
"existence, readability, writability and executability of *path*, "
"respectively."
msgstr ""
"Hodnoty k predan jako *mode* parametr :func:`access` k testovani existence, "
"citelnosti, zapisatelnosti a proveditlnosti *path*, respektive."

#: ../../library/os.rst:2121
msgid "Change the current working directory to *path*."
msgstr "Zmeni aktualni pracovni adresare na *path*."

#: ../../library/os.rst:2123
msgid ""
"This function can support :ref:`specifying a file descriptor <path_fd>`.  "
"The descriptor must refer to an opened directory, not an open file."
msgstr ""
"Tato funkce muze podporovat :ref:`specifikaci deskriptoru souboru "
"<path_fd>`. Deskriptor se musi vztahovat na otevreny adresare, ne otevreny "
"soubor."

#: ../../library/os.rst:2126
msgid ""
"This function can raise :exc:`OSError` and subclasses such as "
":exc:`FileNotFoundError`, :exc:`PermissionError`, and "
":exc:`NotADirectoryError`."
msgstr ""
"Tato funkce muze vyvolan :exc:`OSError` a podtridy jako "
":exc:`FileNotFoundError`, :exc:`PermissionError` a "
":exc:`NotADirectoryError`."

#: ../../library/os.rst:2129 ../../library/os.rst:2267
msgid ""
"Raises an :ref:`auditing event <auditing>` ``os.chdir`` with argument "
"``path``."
msgstr ""
"Vyvola :ref:`auditni udalost <auditing>` ``os.chdir`` s argumentem ``path``."

#: ../../library/os.rst:2131
msgid ""
"Added support for specifying *path* as a file descriptor on some platforms."
msgstr ""
"Pridana podpora pro specifikaci *path* jako deskriptor souboru na nekterych "
"platformach."

